Abadia,f,,Portuguese (Brazilian),/a.ba.ˈd͡ʒi.ɐ/(Brazilian Portuguese),,,,,,,"Derived from Portuguese abadia ""abbey"", this name is usually used in reference to the title of the Virgin Mary Nossa Senhora da Abadia ""Our Lady of the Abbey"". The title itself goes back to a Marian apparition near the Abadia do Bouro in Braga, Portugal. Nossa Senhora da Abadia is the patron saint of Uberaba."
