Abd al-Mu'min,m,عَبْد الْمُؤْمِن(Arabic),Arabic,/ʕab.doool.mooo.ˈmin/,,,,,,,"Means ""servant of the believer"" from Arabic from Arabic عبد (ʿabd) meaning ""servant"" and مُؤْمِن (muʔmin) meaning ""mu'min, believer"". This was the name of a prominent member of the Almohad movement who was the founder and first caliph of the Almohad Caliphate."
