Aberkios,m,Ἀβέρκιος(Ancient Greek),Late Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly derived from Latin aberceo meaning ""to keep away, ward off"". This name was borne by a 2nd-century saint of Phrygia in Asia Minor, a bishop and wonderworker of Hieropolis who is the subject (and probable author) of an early Christian inscription."
