Abgar,m,ܒܓܪ(Syriac)|ܐܲܒ݂ܓܲܪ(Assyrian Neo-Aramaic)|Աբգար(Armenian),Ancient Aramaic|Assyrian|Armenian|History,,,,,,,,"From Classical Syriac ܐܒܓܪܐ (abgara) meaning ""lame"". This was the name of 10 rulers of the ancient kingdom of Osroene, including Abgar V Ukkama, said to be one of the first Christian kings, having been converted by Thaddeus of Edessa, one of the seventy disciples.A notable modern bearer of the name is Assyrian-Swedish professional footballer Abgar Barsom (b. 1977)."
