Abishalom,m,אֲבִישָׁלוֹם(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""my father is peace"" or ""father of peace"", derived from Hebrew אָב (ʾav) ""father"" and שָׁלוֹם (shalom) ""peace"". (Also compare Absalom, which lacks the letter י (i) ""my"" suffixed to the first element.) This name belongs to the father-in-law of King Rehoboam and maternal grandfather of King Abijam in the Old Testament."
