Ablayar,m,Аблаяр(Uzbek Cyrillic),Uzbek (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. It looks like this is a compound name, of which the first element is probably either 'Abla or Ablay. The second element might possibly be the Persian noun یار (yar) meaning ""friend, companion"" as well as ""assistant, helper"" (see Elyar).This name is archaic in Uzbekistan today, but its modern forms Oblayor and Obloyor are still used there, albeit rarely."
