Abo,m,აბო(Georgian),Georgian (Rare)|East Frisian,/ɑ.bɔ/,,,,,,,"The usage of this name started in honour of the 8th-century saint Abo of Tiflis, who was of Arab origin and martyred for having converted from Islam to Christianity.His original name was Abu, though some Georgian sources claim that it may have been Habib instead, since its short form is Habo, which is very similar to Abo."
