Afagddu,m,,Welsh Mythology,/a.ˈvaɡ.ðiː/,,,,,,,"Derived from Welsh y fagddu meaning ""utter darkness"". In Welsh legends this was originally a nickname belonging to the Arthurian warrior Morfran, who was so ugly and hairy that when he fought at the battle of Camlann, none of the other warriors struck him because they thought he was a devil; later legends transferred the character's ugliness and nickname to a brother, Afagddu."
