Afallach,m,,Welsh Mythology,/av.ˈaɬ.aχ/,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Middle Welsh afall ""apple"". This may be cognate with Abelio or Abellio, the name of a Gaulish god, which is thought to come from Proto-Celtic *aballo- ""apple"" (also the source of the mythical place name Avalon). According to a medieval Welsh triad, Afallach was the father of the goddess Modron. The 12th-century chronicler William of Malmesbury called him Avalloc and said he lived in Avalon along with his daughters."
