Agapomenos,m,Ἀγαπωμενός(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""one who is loved"", from Greek ἀγαπάω (agapao) meaning ""to love, be fond of, show affection for"" (see agape)."
Agaptolemos,m,Ἀγαπτόλεμος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Greek ἀγάπη (agape) meaning ""love"" and the Epic form of πόλεμος (polemos) meaning ""war"". This was the name of a son of Aegyptus in Greek mythology."
Agara,f,,Basque (Archaic)|Biblical Basque,,,,,,,,Basque form of Hagar.
Agares,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. This is the name of a demon who appears in several works on demonology, including the 17th-century grimoire The Lesser Key of Solomon (author unknown), the Pseudomonarchia Daemonum (1563) by Dutch physician Johann Weyer and the Dictionnaire Infernal (1818) by French occultist Jacques Collin de Plancy."
