Agatuccia,f,,Medieval Italian|Italian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Medieval Italian diminutive of Agata, as -uccia is an Italian feminine diminutive suffix.A known bearer of this name was Agata ""Agatuccia"" de Pesce (also Pesci), the mistress of king Martin I of Sicily (1374-1409)."
