Aginric,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Germanic element agin (which is an extended form of ag - see Agmund and compare Egino) combined with rîcja ""powerful, strong, mighty."" The second element is also closely related to Celtic rîg or rix and Gothic reiks, which all mean ""king, ruler."""
