Agnetis,f,,Dutch (Rare)|English (Archaic)|German (Archaic),ahkh-NAY-tis(Dutch),,,,,,,"From Latin Agnetis, which is the genitive of the third declension of Agnes, the latinized form of the Greek name Hagne.In the Netherlands, this has been used as a Latin form of Agnes (thus basically making it a latinization of a latinization) since at least late medieval times."
