Agnimitra,m,अग्निमित्र(Sanskrit),Sanskrit|Literature,/ˈɐɡ.n̪i.mit̪.ɾɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""friend of fire"" from Sanskrit अग्नि (agni) meaning ""fire"" and मित्र (mitra) meaning ""friend"". This was the name of a ruler of the Shunga Empire, which existed in the 2nd century BCE in north-central India. He was featured as one of the titular characters in the play Mālavikāgnimitram by 5th-century author Kalidasa, in which he falls in love with his chief queen's handmaiden Malavika."
