Agrios,m,Ἄγριος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/ˈæɡ.ri.əs/(English)|/ˈa.ɣri.os/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""wild, savage, harsh; living in the fields"" in Ancient Greek. This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including one of the Giants (or Gigantes) killed in the Gigantomachy, a half-bear son of Polyphonte, a centaur, a suitor of Penelope, and a Calydonian prince."
