Agrotora,f,,Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"This was an epithet of the Greek goddess Artemis, under which title she was regarded as the patron goddess of hunters. Conceivably related to Greek ἄγρᾱ (agra) ""hunt, catch"" and the name of the Brythonic war goddess Agrona, from old Celtic agro ""battle, carnage""."
