Aguri,,"亜久里, 安久里, 阿久里, 亜久利, 安久利, 阿久利, 亜久梨, 亜久理, 亜久莉(Japanese Kanji)|あぐり(Japanese Hiragana)|アグリ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,AH-GUU-ṘEE,,,,,,,"As a unisex name, this name combines 亜 (a, tsu.gu) meaning ""Asia, come after, rank next,"" 安 (an, yasu, yasu.i, yasu.maru, yasu.raka, a) meaning ""cheap, low, peaceful, rested"" or 阿 (a, o, omone.ru, kuma) meaning ""corner, flatter, nook"" with 久 (kyuu, ku, hisa.shii) meaning ""long time"" & 里 (ri, sato) meaning ""parent's home, ri (unit of distance - equal to 3.927 km), village.""As a masculine name, it's the same except that the last kanji is replaced by 利 (ri, ki.ku) which means ""advantage, benefit, profit, gain.""As a feminine name, it combines 亜 with 久 & 梨 (ri, nashi) meaning ""pear tree,"" 理 (ri, kotowari) meaning ""justice, logic, reason, truth"" or 莉 (rai, ri, rei), part of 茉莉 (matsuri) meaning ""jasmine.""One (male) bearer of this name is former racing driver Aguri Suzuki (鈴木 亜久里) (1960-)."
