Ahaziah,m,אֲחַזְיָהוּ(Ancient Hebrew),Ancient Hebrew|Biblical,,,,,,,,"From Hebrew אֲחַזְיָהוּ (ʼĂḥazyāhū) meaning ""held by Yahweh"", derived from the roots אֲחַזְ ('ahaz) meaning "" to hold, to grasp"" and יְהוֹ (yeho) referring to the Hebrew God. The name Jehoahaz is derived from the same roots in reverse order. This was the name of two kings, one in Israel and one in Judah."
