Ahimelech,m,אחימלך(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""my brother is king"" in Hebrew, from אָח (ʾaḥ) meaning ""brother"" combined with י (i) ""my"" and מֶלֶךְ (meleḵ) ""king"". This is the name of several characters in the Old Testament, including a high priest of Israel who is wrongly executed for treason on King Saul's orders."
