Ahisamach,m,אחיסמך(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""brother of support"" or ""my brother supports"", derived from the Hebrew noun אָח (ʾaḥ) meaning ""brother"" (combined with the letter י (i) ""my"", thus ""my brother"" or ""brother of"") and the verb סמך (samak) ""to support, to uphold"". In the Old Testament Ahisamach of the tribe of Dan was the father of Aholiab."
