Aithalion,m,Αἰθαλίων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek αἰθαλίων (aithalion) meaning ""swarthy, dusky; browned, toasted"". It is also possible that this name means ""son of Aithalos"", in which case it consists of the name Aithalos and the patronymic suffix -ίων (-ion)."
Aithalos,m,Αἴθαλος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/ǎi̯.tʰa.los/(Attic Greek)|/ˈɛ.θa.los/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from either Ancient Greek αἴθαλος (aithalos) meaning ""thick smoke, smoky flame"" or αἰθάλη (aithale) meaning ""soot"", both of which ultimately derived from αἰθος (aithos) meaning ""fire, burning heat"", which itself is derived from αἴθω (aitho) meaning ""to ignite, to light (up), to kindle, to burn""."
