Ajisai,f,紫陽花(Japanese Kanji)|あじさい(Japanese Hiragana)|アジサイ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese,AH-JYEE-SIE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 紫陽花 (ajisai) meaning ""hydrangea"" which comes from combining 紫 (murasaki) meaning ""purple, violet"", 陽 (yō) meaning ""light, sun, male"", and 花 (hana, ka) meaning ""flower"". Other kanji or combinations of kanji can also form this name."
