Alaksandu,m,,Hittite (Archaic),,,,,,,,Ancient Hittite form of Alexandros (see Alexander). This was the name of a Wilusan king who signed a treaty with the Hittite kings Muwatalli II and Mursuli II.
Alakshmi,f,অলক্ষ্মী(Bengali),Indian (Rare)|Hinduism,,,,,,,,"The name of the older sister of Lakshmi and the Hindu goddess of misfortune. She is sometimes viewed, according to one source, as another avatar of a form of the goddess Kali. It is derived from a, a negative participle, and the name Lakshmi, meaning ""one who is not the goddess Lakshmi""."
