Alara,f,,"Turkish (Modern)|Turkic Mythology (Rare, ?)|Breton (Rare)|Yoruba|History",ah-LAH-rah(Turkish),,,,,,,"Used by Refik Halit Karay for one of the main characters in his 1950-51 serialized novel 2000 Yılın Sevgilisi (Sweetheart of the Year 2000). Karay based the name on that of Alara Castle, a medieval fortress near Alanya in southern Turkey.However, it is sometimes claimed to be a Turkish rendering of Elere or Elire, the name of a character in some Siberian tales, or to be the name of a beautiful water fairy in Turkic mythology, who is said to live in the lakes and rivers of the Caspian basin and to grant wishes for those she deems worthy; she is also able to repair broken hearts and make them capable of love again."
