Alcimede,f,Ἀλκιμέδη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἀλκή (alke) meaning ""strength, prowess"" and μήδεα (medea) meaning ""plans, counsel, cunning"". Alternatively, it could be a feminine form of Alcimedon, the second element instead being μέδω (medo) meaning ""to protect, rule over"". This was the name of the mother of the hero Jason in Greek mythology."
