Aldhanab,m,,Astronomy,/ˈæl.də.næb/,,,,,,,"This is the name of the star Gamma Gruis in the constellation Grus. The name Aldhanab comes from Al Dhanab, from the Arabic الذنب al-dhanab meaning ""the tail (of the Southern Fish)""."
Aldhelm,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Means ""old helmet"", derived from the Germanic elements ald ""old"" and helm ""helmet, protection"". However, it should be noted that there are also various cases where this name is a variant form of Adalhelm, due to metathesis.This name was borne by an Anglo-Saxon saint from the 8th century AD. His original name was actually Ealdhelm, but it was often variantly written as Aldhelm."
