Alegenor,m,Ἀλεγήνωρ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from either the Epic Greek verb ἀλέγω (alego) meaning ""to have a care, to mind, to heed"" or the adjective ἀλεγεινός (alegeinos), which is the Epic Greek form of ἀλγεινός (algeinos) meaning ""painful, grievous"". The second element of this name is derived from the Greek noun ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man"".In Greek mythology, Alegenor is the father of the Boeotian warriors Clonius and Promachus, who both fought and died in the Trojan War."
