Alemande,f,,Judeo-French|Judeo-Anglo-Norman,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old French alemande, the feminine form of the adjective alemant ""German"". This name might originally have been given to someone of German ancestry or to someone whose ancestors came from the town of Allemagne in Normandy (present-day Fleury-sur-Orne)."
