Aletes,m,Ἀλήτης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""wanderer, vagabond, rover"" in Ancient Greek. This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including the youngest son of Clytemnestra, who was killed by his half-brother Orestes."
