Aletheia,f,Ἀλήθεια(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀλήθεια (aletheia) meaning ""truth"". (Compare English Alethea.) According to some Greek myths she was the personification of truth, a daughter of Zeus and one of the nurses to Apollo."
