Alexandrides,m,Ἀλεξανδρίδης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Alexandros"" in Greek, derived from the name Alexandros combined with the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).A known bearer of this name was the ancient Greek historian Alexandrides of Delphi."
Alexandrína,f,,Icelandic (Archaic),,,,,,,,Icelandic form of Alexandrina.
