Alexandrite,f,,English (Rare)|Filipino (Rare),/ˌæl.ɪɡ.ˈzæn.dɹaɪt/(English),,,,,,,"From the name of a chrysoberyl that displays a colour change depending on the light source, named after the Russian tsar Alexander II of Russia (1818-1881)."
