Alishba,f,"علشبه, علیشبہ(Urdu)",Urdu (Modern),,,,,,,,"Modern Urdu name of uncertain meaning, which became popular in Pakistan in the 1980s. It might be formed from Arabic عليّ (ʿalīy) ""high, exalted"" and shobh allegedly meaning ""appearance, likeness"". Alternatively it may be derived from Elisheba (compare Syriac ܐܠܝܫܒܥ (Elişbah)), the name of Aaron's wife in the Old Testament and of John the Baptist's mother in the New Testament, but traditionally Elizabeth was Ilshaba or Ilshabet in Urdu."
