Alizarin,,,Literature,/ə.ˈlɪzəɹɪn/,,,,,,,"From alizarin crimson, the English name of a shade of red. The color is named after a red dye originally obtained from the root of the madder plant, ultimately from Arabic al-usara meaning ""the juice"". This was used for a male character in the romance novel 'Pandora' by Jilly Cooper."
