Alkandros,m,Ἄλκανδρος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek αλκη (alke) meaning ""strength"" combined with ανδρος (andros) meaning ""of a man"". This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including a Molossian prince whose entire family was turned into birds by Zeus to save them from a fire, Alkandros becoming a wren, and a Lycian soldier in the Trojan war."
Alkanor,m,Ἀλκάνωρ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἀλκή (alke) meaning ""strength"" combined with the Greek noun ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man""."
Alkawari,f,,Indigenous Australian|Pitjantjatjara,,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown (but from Pitjantjatjara language).A known bearer of this name was Alkawari Dawson (c. 1930-2010), an Australian Aboriginal painter who was also the first wife of fellow artist Nyakul Dawson (c. 1935-2007)."
