Allogenes,m,,Gnosticism,,,,,,,,"Allogenes (from Greek Allogenēs, meaning “stranger” or “of another race/kind”) is a revelatory figure in Sethian Gnostic literature, most prominently the protagonist of the text Allogenes from the Nag Hammadi library. He is portrayed as a spiritual seeker who receives visionary instruction from higher divine beings, especially concerning the nature of the ultimate, unknowable God and the structure of the transcendent realms. In related texts such as Zostrianos, the name also appears as a title or designation for an enlightened figure who has become “other” to the material world through gnosis. Allogenes thus represents the ideal Gnostic initiate; through revelation and contemplation, he transcends the cosmos and returns to the divine source."
