Alniyat,,,Astronomy,/æl.ˈnaɪ.jæt/,,,,,,,"Sigma Scorpii and Tau Scorpii together bore the traditional name Al Niyat (or Alniyat) derived from the Arabic النياط al-niyāţ ""the arteries"" and referring to their position flanking the star Antares, the scorpion's heart, with Sigma Scorpii just to the north."
