Alope,f,Ἀλόπη(Ancient Greek),Apache|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Borne by the first wife of the Apache chief Geronimo (1829-1909), daughter of Noposo, from the Nedni-Chiricahua band of Apache. She and her three children with Geronimo were killed by Mexican raiders."
Alor,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),/a.lɔʁ/(French),,,,,,,"Alor of Quimper was a Breton saint in the 5th century AD and bishop of Quimper in Brittany, France. He is the patron saint of aleviners, foals and horses, and was also invoked to attract rain."
