Alsafi,f,,Astronomy,/æl.ˈseɪ.fi/,,,,,,,"This is the name of the star Sigma Draco is in the constellation Draco. It bore the traditional name Alsafi, derived from the Arabic Athāfi, itself erroneously transcribed from the Arabic plural Athāfiyy, meaning ""the cooking tripods"". This refers to the tripods used by nomads for open-air cooking."
