Alulim,m,𒀉𒇻𒅆(Sumerian Cuneiform),Sumerian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""horn of the red deer"" or ""seed of the red deer"" in Sumerian, deriving from the elements 𒀉 a (""arm, wing, horn"") and 𒇻𒅆 lulim (""red deer stag""). This was the name of the legendary first king of Sumer, who is thought today to be a mythological figure. There is evidence it was never used as an ordinary given name in the Early Dynastic period of Sumer."
