Amaracus,m,Ἀμάρακος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""marjoram (herb)"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, this was the name of a prince (in some later accounts a son of king Cinyras) tasked with preparing royal or sacred perfumes. After dropping a box of perfumes and breaking many, he was transformed into a marjoram plant, which is associated with the goddess Aphrodite."
