Amestris,f,Ἄμηστρις(Ancient Greek),Old Persian (Hellenized),,,,,,,,"Ionic Greek variant of Άμαστρις (Amāstris), the Hellenized form of an Old Persian name, perhaps from a hypothetic name like *Amāstrī- (composed of the elements *ama- ""strength, strong"" and *strī- ""woman""). It could be connected to the biblical name Esther, both perhaps derived from the Akkadian Ummu-Ishtar ""Ishtar is (my) mother"" (or Ammu-Ishtar). Alternatively it could be derived from an Old Persian word meaning ""friend"". It was borne by the wife of Xerxes and mother of Artaxerxes."
