Amoret,f,,Literature,a-mor-et|a-mor-ay,,,,,,,"Perhaps based on the Italian word amoretto which is a representation of Cupid in a work of art. The word is based on amore meaning ""love"" combined with a diminutive suffix.This name was used by Edmund Spenser in his poem 'The Faerie Queene' (1590), where it belongs to a sister of Belphoebe who allegorically represents married love and chastity."
