Ámundi,m,,Old Norse|Icelandic,,,,,,,,"Old Norse name, in which the first element Á- may be derived from Old Norse *ana- ""all"" or agi ""awe, terror"" or *ag- ""point, weapon point"". The second element -mundi is a weak side-form of mundr, itself derived from Old West Scandinavian *-munduR meaning ""protector"" or possibly from Old Icelandic mundr meaning ""gift"". Also compare Agmundr."
