Amzi,m,אמצי(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,AHM-tsee(Biblical English)|AM-zie(Biblical English),,,,,,,"Probably Hebrew, and may mean ""my strength"". 'In the Bible it occurs only once, in a genealogy... It appears regularly at Princeton in the period 1810-60, but not at Harvard. Apparently Amzi represents a development in the Middle Colonies, one which did not reach New England. The contrary is more usual.' A famous bearer was Amzi Chapin, a shape-note music composer and singing master from New England in the early 1800s."
