An Dương Vương,m,,Vietnamese Mythology|History,/ʔaːn˧˧ zɨəŋ˧˧ vɨəŋ˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/ʔaːn˧˧ jɨəŋ˧˧ vɨəŋ˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/ʔaːŋ˧˧ jɨəŋ˧˧ vɨəŋ˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"Means ""King of An Dương"", from Sino-Vietnamese 安陽 (an dương) and 王 (vương) meaning ""king"". He was the king of Âu Lạc, an ancient Yue kingdom, and the leader of the Âu Việt tribes, uniting them with the Lạc Việt. His real name was Thục Phán (蜀泮). He was the father of Mỵ Châu. Although he was a real historical person, he is the subject of many legends around the founding of Vietnam."
