Anguillette,f,,Folklore,,,,,,,,"Means ""little eel"" in French (a diminutive of French anguille ""eel""). This name is borne by the titular character of the fairy tale ""Anguillette"" (1697) by Henriette-Julie de Murat. Anguillette is a fairy who takes the form of an eel, and is rescued by a princess while in this form."
