Annea,f,,Celtic Mythology|Swedish (Rare)|Norwegian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Annea was a goddess worshipped in the province of Cuneo in the southwest of the Piedmont region of Italy. The origin and meaning of her name are uncertain, it has, however, been suggested that it might be related to Celtic ann- ""mother"" (compare the name of the Irish goddess Anu)."
