Antandre,f,Ἀντάνδρη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἄντανδρος (antandros) meaning ""instead of a man, substitute"", composed of ἀντί (anti) ""against, compared to, like"" and ἀνδρός (andros) ""of a man"" (compare Antenor). Antandre was an Amazon warrior in Greek mythology, one of Penthesilea's twelve companions at Troy."
