Anthelia,f,Ἀνθήλεια(Ancient Greek),"Coptic (Archaic)|Greek Mythology (Latinized)|American (South, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Means ""opposite the sun, looking east"" or ""reflecting the sun"", derived from Ancient Greek ἀντί (anti) meaning ""against, opposed, compared to, like"" and ἥλιος (helios) meaning ""sun"". In Greek mythology, Anthelia was one of the fifty daughters of Danaus, murdering her husband, Cisseus, on their wedding night."
