Anthus,m,Ἄνθος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek ἄνθος (anthos) meaning ""flower, blossom, bloom"". This was also the name of a kind of small bird, according to legend named after the mythical character Anthus, a son of Hippodameia and Autonous who was eaten by his father’s starving horses when he denied them pasture and turned into a bird by the gods out of pity for his family."
