Anudeya,,,Obscure,,,,,,,,"From the Sanskrit word अनुदेय (anudeya) meaning ""gift"", from अनु (anu) ""away, after"" and दा (dā) ""to give"" (i.e. ""to give back"" or ""to give in turn""). This was used as a 'sannyas' name by followers of the controversial Indian spiritual teacher Bhagwan Shree Rajneesh (1931-1990), also known as Osho. It was customary for new followers, or sannyasins, to receive a new name from Osho during initiation ceremonies."
