Aono,f,"青乃, 蒼乃, 碧野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-O-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 青 (ao) ""blue"", 蒼 (ao) meaning ""blue, green"", or 碧 (ao) meaning ""green, blue"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle or 野 (no) meaning ""plain, wilderness, field"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Aopeng,m,"翱鹏, 翱怦(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 翱 (áo) meaning ""soar, roam"" and 鹏 (péng), the name of a mythological bird or 怦 (pēng) meaning ""eager, ardent""."
Aoqin,,"奥琴, 傲钦(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 奥 (ào) meaning ""mysterious, obscure, profound"" or 傲 (ào) meaning ""proud, haughty"" and 琴 (qín), a type of Chinese lute or 钦 (qīn) meaning ""respect, admire; respectful""."
