Apama,f,Ἀπάμα(Ancient Greek),Old Persian,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, probably related to Avestan apama- ""the latest"", hence ""the youngest (child), nestling"". This was the name of Apama, the first Queen of the Seleucid Empire, and wife of Seleucus I Nicator. She was sometimes known as Apama I or Apame I. Several towns were named Apamea after Apama I. Other bearers of this name include Apama II, a Seleucid Princess, and her niece Apama III."
