Apanoub,m,"Ⲁⲡⲁⲛⲟⲩⲃ, Ⲁⲡⲁⲛⲩⲃ(Coptic)",Coptic,,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Coptic apa Anoub, where apa means ""father"" and Anoub is the Coptic form of Anubis. The name thus essentially means ""father Anubis"". However, it may also be possible that the name is a more extended form of Panoub."
Apanuugak,m,,Inuit Mythology,,,,,,,,"In Inuit mythology, Apanuugak is a culture hero who was sometimes depicted as an error-prone warrior who lives to old age and sometimes as a dastardly villain."
