Appias,f,,Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derivative of Appius, or possibly means ""of Appia"" in Latin (Appia being a town in Phrygia Major). In Roman mythology, Appias was a naiad of the Appian Well or fountain of Aqua Appia, whose waters gushed forth near the Temple of Venus Genetrix in the Forum of Iulius Caesar, Rome."
Appie,m,,Dutch,/ˈɑ.pi/,,,,,,,"Diminutive of Albert and Albertus. A notable bearer of this name was the Dutch author Appie Baantjer (1923-2010), who was well-known for his detective fiction.In the Netherlands, the premium supermarket chain Albert Heijn (named after its late founder) is colloquially referred to as (the) Appie."
