Apranik,f,,Middle Persian|History,,,,,,,,"The name of a commander of the Sasanian army against the invading Arab-Muslim forces during the reign of Yazdegerd III (632-651 CE). After the Sasanian defeat, she continued to the resistance, fighting a guerilla war until she was killed in battle."
Aprasion,m,აფრასიონ(Georgian),Georgian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Georgian sources state that this name is of Persian origin and means ""angry, wrathful"" and ""ferocious, truculent"". This indicates that Aprasion might be the Georgian form of افراسیاب (Afrasiyab) (see Afrasiab), probably via its archaic Georgian form აფრასიობ (Aprasiob) or აფრასიობი (Aprasiobi).A notable bearer of this name was the Georgian revolutionary Aprasion Merkviladze (1871-1907)."
Aprelina,f,Апрелина(Russian),Soviet,,,,,,,,"From Russian апрель (aprel'), meaning ""April"", referring to Lenin's month of birth and/or April Theses, one of Lenin's works."
Apres,m,Ապրես(Armenian),Armenian (Eastern),[ɑp.ˈɾɛs](Eastern Armenian),,,,,,,"Means ""well done!, good job!"" in Armenian."
Apreshum,f,Ապրեշում(Armenian),Armenian (Archaic),/ɑ.pɾɛ.ˈʃum/,,,,,,,"From Persian ابریشم (abrīsham) meaning ""silk"". This is a cognate of Persian Abrisham."
Apri,,,Indonesian,/ˈa.pri/,,,,,,,From the name of the month of April.
Apriani,f,,Indonesian,/a.pri.ˈa.ni/,,,,,,,"From the name of the month of April, usually used as a given name for a girl born in April."
