Arahan,m,အရဟံ(Burmese),History,/ʔə.jə.hàɰ̃/(Burmese),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit अर्हत् (arhat) meaning ""deserving, entitled to, worthy, venerable"". This was the name of an 11th-century Burmese monk who helped to stabilize the presence of Theravada Buddhism in Southeast Asia."
