Arara,,"アララ(Japanese Katakana)|亜羅羅, 愛麗玲, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-RA-RA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 亜 (a) meaning ""second, Asia"" or 愛 (a) meaning ""love, affection"", 羅 (ra) meaning ""gauze, thin silk"" or 麗 (ra) meaning ""lovely, beautiful, graceful, resplendent"" combined with 羅 (ra) meaning ""gauze, thin silk"" or 玲 (ra) meaning ""sound of jewels"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
