Arbër,m,,Albanian,AHR-bər,,,,,,,"The name represents the demonym of Albania as it used to be called in Medieval times, ""Arberi/a"". It ultimately goes back to the Albanian tribal name Arbër/Arbëreshë.Equivalently, the name could be the toponym of the Illyrian tribe of ""Abri"" who inhabited part of modern day Albania.The name is popularly held to be derived from Albanian arë ""field; cropland; croft""."
