Arbor,,,English|Albanian (Rare),/ˈɑɹ.bɚ/,,,,,,,"Middle English (also denoting a lawn or flower bed) from Old French erbier, from erbe ‘grass, herb’, from Latin herba. The phonetic change to ar- (common in words having er- before a consonant) was assisted by association with Latin arbor ‘tree’."
