Arcas,m,Ἀρκάς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/ˈɑːr.kəs/(English)|/ar.ˈkas/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""Arcadian"" in Ancient Greek, possibly related to ἄρκτος (arktos) meaning ""bear"". In Greek mythology this was the name of an eponymous king of Arcadia, a son of Zeus and Callisto. In some variants of myth, Arcas is transformed into the constellation Boötes when his mother becomes Ursa Major."
