Arcesius,m,Ἀρκείσιος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἀρκέω (arkeo) meaning ""to ward off, defend, hold out, be strong enough"" or ""to assist, succour, suffice"". In Greek mythology, this was the name of a king of Ithaca, of varying parentage between myths; in some he is the son of Zeus and Euryodeia, in others he is the son of King Cephalus and either Procris or a bear transformed into a human woman."
Arceus,m,,Obscure,[ˈɑɹk.i.əs](English),,,,,,,"From the Pokémon character Arceus, whose name comes from the combination of the Greek word αρχή (arkhé), ""origin"", and the Latin word deus (god). In the game lore, Arceus is the original Pokémon who created the universe. This name was given to 7 boys in 2022 in the United States coinciding with the release of the video game 'Pokemon Legends: Arceus'."
