Aréthuse,f,,Greek Mythology (Gallicized),,,,,,,,French form of Arethusa.
Aretias,m,Ἀρητιάς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from the name of the god Ares. This was the name of the father of Nissus of Dulichium in the Odyssey. It’s also an ancient name of Giresun Island, a small island on the southeastern coast of Black Sea that was sacred to Ares."
Aretius,m,,Medieval English,,,,,,,,Possibly a variant of Aretias.
