Argyra,f,Ἀργυρᾶ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˈɑːr.dʒɪ.rə/(English),,,,,,,"Feminine form of Argyros ""silver"". According to Pausanias, Argyra was the nymph of a well in Achaea, whose human lover Selemnos died of grief after she abandoned him. Aphrodite took pity on Selemnos and changed him into a river."
Argyri,f,Αργυρή(Greek),Greek,,,,,,,,"Dialect form of Argyro found in Pontus, Epirus, Silata, Cappadocia, Western Macedonia and Skiathos."
