Aristogenes,m,Ἀριστογένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/a.ris.to.ɡé.nɛːs/(Attic Greek)|/a.ris.to.ˈʝe.nis/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with γενής (genes) meaning ""born"" or ""of a kind"". This name was borne by two ancient Greek physicians from the 3rd century BC."
