Aristokrates,m,Ἀριστοκράτης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Greek form of Aristocrates.
Aristokreon,m,Ἀριστοκρέων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with κρέων (kreon) meaning ""king, master, ruler"" (also compare Kreon)."
Aristokritos,m,Ἀριστόκριτος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Greek form of Aristocritus.
Aristolaos,m,Ἀριστόλαος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with the Greek noun λαός (laos) meaning ""(the) people"".This was the name of a Greek painter from the 4th century BC."
Aristolaus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Aristolaos.
Aristoleon,m,Ἀριστολέων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with the Greek noun λέων (leon) meaning ""lion""."
Aristolochos,m,Ἀριστόλοχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἀριστόλοχος (aristolochos) meaning ""well-born"", which consists of the Greek adjective ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with the Greek noun λόχος (lochos) meaning ""childbirth"" as well as ""ambush"". Through the latter meaning, the word later came to signify a tactical sub unit of the ancient Greek army. It is the connection to combat and the military that usually made the ancient Greeks want to incorporate the word into given names (see names like Amphilochos, Astylochos and Hippolochos), but in some cases an exception was made, and this name is one of them."
Aristolochus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Aristolochos. This name was borne by an Olympic victor from 344 BC.In Greek mythology, Aristolochus was one of the men who fought against Troy in the Trojan War."
Aristomachos,m,Ἀριστόμαχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""best battle"", derived from Greek ἄριστος (aristos) ""best"" combined with Greek μάχη (mache) ""battle."""
Aristomachus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Aristomachos. In Greek mythology, Aristomachus is the name of one of Heracles' descendants."
Aristomeda,f,Ἀριστομέδα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from ἄριστος (aristos) ""best"" and μέδομαι (medomai) ""to be mindful of"". She was a woman that offered her tithe to the goddess Demeter."
Aristomenes,m,Ἀριστομένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" and μένος (menos) meaning ""mind, courage, strength, spirit""."
Aristomenis,m,Αριστομένης(Greek),Greek,,,,,,,,Modern Greek form of Aristomenes.
Aristonax,m,Ἀριστώναξ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" combined with the Greek noun ἄναξ (anax) meaning ""master, lord, chief""."
