Arjumand,f,আরজুমান্দ(Bengali)|ارجمند(Urdu),Urdu|Indian (Muslim)|Bengali (Muslim),,,,,,,,"From Classical Persian آرزومند (ārzumand) meaning ""wishful"", from آرزو (ārzu) ""wish"" (compare modern Persian Arezou) and the possessive suffix ـمند (-mand). A famous bearer was Arjumand Banu Begum (1593-1631), better known by her title Mumtaz Mahal, the chief consort of the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan for whom he built the Taj Mahal."
