Arminas,m,,Lithuanian,[ˈɐrʲ.mʲɪ.nɐs],,,,,,,"This name can be the Lithuanian form of the German name Armin as well as be an independent, authentic Lithuanian name. In the case of the latter, the name consists of Lithuanian ar meaning ""also, too, as well (as)"" combined with the Lithuanian verb minėti meaning ""to celebrate"" as well as ""to remember, to commemorate"".A known bearer of this name is the Lithuanian former soccer player Arminas Narbekovas (b. 1965)."
