Armonía,f,,Spanish (Rare),/aɾ.mo.ˈni.a/,,,,,,,"Means ""harmony"" in Spanish. This name was brought to public attention by the novel 'Sembrando Flores' (1906) by Catalan anarchist Juan Montseny Carret, whose main characters are named Floreal and Armonía, and thus it came to be used by anarchist parents who were eager to reject traditional names during the Second Spanish Republic (1931-1939)."
