Arrhabaeus,m,Ἀρραβαῖος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History,,,,,,,,"Latinized form of the Ancient Greek given name Ἀρραβαῖος (Arrhabaios), which is probably a hellenised form of a Macedonian name of uncertain etymology. Perhaps related to the Proto-Indo-European root *wérsēn meaning ""virile man"" or ""male animal, bull"", or to Ancient Greek ἄραβος (arabos) meaning ""gnashing, chattering (of teeth); ringing, rattling"". This was the name of a king of Lynkestis who lived in the 5th century BC."
