Artaynte,f,,Old Persian (Hellenized),,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. This name's only bearer was the wife of the crown prince Darius, who later committed adultery with Xerxes I. This name may be related to the similar masculine name Artayntes."
Artayntes,m,Ἀρταΰντης(Ancient Greek),Old Persian (Hellenized),,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. This name was borne by a commander of Xerxes I, who almost killed Xerxes' brother Masistes in an argument, but Masistes was saved by Xenagoras, who was given rule of Cilicia because of this. This name may be related to the Old Persian feminine name Artaynte."
