Artemiche,f,Ἀρτεμίχη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly derived from the name of the goddess Artemis, or perhaps the Ancient Greek word ἀρτεμής (artemes) meaning ""safe, unharmed, perfectly healthy"". In Greek mythology, Artemiche was a young noblewoman whose family angered Apollo, and was turned into a bird by Artemis and Leto to save her from death."
