Artimpasa,f,Αρτιμπασα(Ancient Greek),Scythian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Likely deriving from the name of the goddess Arti, with the elements paya (""pasture"") and pati (""lord"") (both of which stem from a common root). This was the name of a major Scythian goddess of fertility, warfare, and sovereignty. She was equated by Herodotus of Halicarnassus with Aphrodite Ourania."
