Artystone,f,Ἀρτυστώνη(Ancient Greek),Old Persian (Hellenized),,,,,,,,"Greek form of the Old Persian name *Ṛtastūnā meaning ""pillar of Ṛta, the deified Truth"", derived from 𐎠𐎼𐎫 (arta) ""true"" and‎ 𐎿𐎬𐎢𐎴𐎠 (stūnā) ""pillar, column"". According to Herodotus this was the name of one of the daughters of Cyrus the Great, and consequently a sister (or half-sister) of Atossa. She was married to Darius and was the mother of Arsames and Gobryas."
