Arvaidas,m,,Lithuanian,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Lithuanian ar meaning ""also, too, as well (as)"". The second element is derived from the old Lithuanian verb vaidyti meaning ""to visit, to appear"", which is related to the modern Lithuanian verb vaidentis meaning ""to haunt"" as well as ""to appear, to see"". Also compare modern Lithuanian vaiduoklis meaning ""ghost, apparition"" and vaidytis meaning ""to quarrel, to wrangle""."
