Asadal,m,아사달(Korean Hangul),Korean (Archaic),/a.sa.dal/,,,,,,,"아사달(阿斯達)(Asadal) is a place name recorded in the Samguk Yusa where it is said that Tangun established and ruled the capital of Gojoseon(? ~ 108 BCE). There is a theory that Joseon(朝鮮) is a semantic transliteration of Asadal.There is also a story about a stonemason from Baekje named Asadal, who is said to have constructed the Seokgatap (Stone Pagoda) of Bulguksa Temple in Silla. He is known through the tale of Asadal and his wife Asanyeo(阿斯女)."
