Asandros,m,Ἄσανδρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἆσαι (asai), an inflected form of ἄω (ao) ""to satiate"" ultimately related to ἥδομαι (hedomai) ""to be pleased, enjoy oneself"", combined with ἀνδρός (andros) ""of a man"". Alternatively, the first element could instead be the related ἀσάω (asao) ""to take a surfeit, to glut oneself""."
