Ashurnasirpal,m,,Ancient Assyrian,,,,,,,,"Means ""the god Ashur is the protector of the heir"" in Assyrian, from the Akkadian Aššur-nāṣir-apli.A noted bearer was Assyrian King Ashurnasirpal I (1049 - 1031 BCE). He is best known for his penitential prayer to Ishtar of Nineveh."
Ashur-uballit,m,,Ancient Assyrian,,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown, but refers to the god Ashur.A noted bearer is Ashur-uballit I (reigned 1365 - 1330 BCE), the first king of the Middle Assyrian Empire (1365 – 1050 BCE). His defeat of the Mitanni king Shuttarna II marks Assyria's independence from this kingdom, and the beginning of its emergence as a powerful empire."
