Ashvini,,"अश्विनी(Sanskrit, Marathi, Hindi)",Astronomy|Marathi|Hindi,/ˈɐɕ.ʋi.n̪iː/(Sanskrit)|/ˈəʃ.ʋɪ.niː/(Hindi),,,,,,,"Feminine form of Sanskrit अश्विन् (aśvin) meaning ""possessed of horses"" (see Ashwin). This is the name of the first nakshatra (lunar mansion) in Hindu astronomy, which roughly corresponds to the head of the Aries constellation. As a given name it is used for both women and men."
