Askalaphos,m,Ἀσκάλαφος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ə.ˈskæ.lə.fəs/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""owl"" in Ancient Greek. This was the name of a custodian of Hades’ underworld orchard in Greek mythology, who was trapped beneath a boulder and then turned into a screech-owl by Demeter in revenge for revealing that Persephone had eaten part of a pomegranate. It was also the name of a son of Ares and Astyoche, twin brother to Ialmenus."
