Asphalion,m,Ἀσφαλίων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἀσφαλής (asphales) meaning ""safe, secure"" as well as ""steadfast, reliable, trustworthy"". In Greek mythology, Asphalion was the name of one of king Menelaus' squires. It was also an epithet of Poseidon."
