Asuelu,m,,Polynesian|Samoan,A-suelu(Samoan),,,,,,,"Possibly a variant of Asaelu, Samoan form of Asahel, or Asielu, Samoan form of Asiel."
Āsugīsalaz,m,,Old Norse,,,,,,,,"Deriving from the Germanic elements ansu- (""god"") and gīslaz (""hostage""). This name is part of an inscription in Proto-Norse on Kragehul I, a lance-shaft from Denmark that has been dated to between 200 and 475 CE."
Asuha,f,"あすは(Japanese Hiragana)|アスハ(Japanese Katakana)|明日葉, 明日羽, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-SOO-HA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"" and 葉 (ha) meaning ""leaf, needle, blade"", or from 飛 (asu) meaning ""to fly"" and 羽 (ha) meaning ""plume, feather"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Asuhi,f,"明日妃, 明日飛, 明日陽, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-SOO-HEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"" combined with 妃 (hi) meaning ""a ruler's wife; queen; empress"", 飛 (hi) meaning ""to fly"" or 陽 (hi) meaning ""light, sun, male"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Asukar,m,"असुकर(Sanskrit, Hindi, Marathi, Nepali)",Sanskrit|Hinduism|Hindi|Indian|Nepali,us- oo- kar(Hinduism)|asukar(Hindi),,,,,,,"""Arduous""; ""not easily done""; ""difficult ""Origin - Sanskrit"
Asuki,f,"あす貴(Kanji/Hiragana)|明日喜, 明日希, 明日貴, 明日輝, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-SOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"" combined with 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Asuko,f,"明日子, 明寿子, 安末子, 安主子, 安寿子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あすこ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,AH-SOO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible as well."
