Ataman,m,,Medieval Turkic (Rare),Ataman,,,,,,,"Used as a title in both Cossacks and Turks.""Ataman"" derives from Gothic ""father of men-warriors"", or Turkic Ata-man, ""father of horsemen"". Cossacks kept in their speech the original meaning of the word, sometimes saying ""father-ataman"" (""bat'ka-ataman""). At war atamans had unlimited power, but in times of peace they were only to carry out decisions of the Cossack Circle and keep order in the community."
