Atete,f,,African Mythology,,,,,,,,"Atete, in Oromo mythology and religion, is a fertility goddess worshipped in the Kafa province in Ethiopia. Her worship was assimilated into the Christian cult of the Virgin Mary, but she's probably the subject of an ancient fertility rite performed by women who collect various sacred plants and throw them into the river known now as 'Astar Yo Mariam' ('The Epiphany of Mary')."
