Atharvan,m,अथर्वन्(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈɐ.t̪ʰɐɾ.ʋɐn̪/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""priest"" in Sanskrit, specifically referring to a priest associated with fire or soma (a type of Vedic ritual drink); the origin of the word itself is unknown. This is the name of a legendary rishi (Hindu sage) who wrote the Atharvaveda, the fourth of the Vedas. It is also an epithet of the rishi Vasishtha and the Hindu god Shiva."
