Atocha,f,,"Spanish (European, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From Spanish atocha meaning ""esparto grass"". This is the name of a local title of Virgin Mary, Nuestra Señora de Atocha (""Our Lady of Atocha"") venerated in Madrid, Spain."
Atogmatogma,m,,Guanche,,,,,,,,Borne by a Guanche prince from Benahoare (modern-day La Palma).
