Atoko,f,"彩十子, 安都子, 亜登子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 彩 (a) meaning ""colour"", 十 (to) meaning ""ten"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atom,,Ատոմ(Armenian),Popular Culture|Armenian,[ɑ.ˈtom](Eastern Armenian),,,,,,,"In the case of film director Atom Egoyan (1960-), it is taken from atom bomb (from Greek atomos meaning ""uncut, unhewn; indivisible"", derived from Greek α, a negative prefix, combined with tomos ""a cutting"", from temnein ""to cut""), given to him by his Armenian-Egyptian parents to mark the completion of Egypt's first nuclear reactor."
Atomu,,"愛富, 亜都夢, 亜斗夢, 亜斗武, 亜富, 亜人夢, 亜十夢, 亜登夢, 亜土夢, 阿斗夢, 阿度夢, 愛斗武(Japanese Kanji)|あとむ(Japanese Hiragana)|アトム(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)",AH-TO-MUU,,,,,,,"Japanese derivation of the English word atom.As a unisex name, it can be used as 愛富, 亜都夢, 亜斗夢 or 亜斗武 with 愛 (ai, ito.shii, o.shimu, kana.shii, mana, me.deru, a) meaning ""affection, love,"" 富 (fu, fuu, tomi, to.mu) meaning ""abundant, enrich, wealth,"" 亜 (a, tsu.gu) meaning ""Asia, come after, rank next,"" 都 (tsu, to, miyako) meaning ""capital, metropolis,"" 斗 (to, tou) meaning ""Big Dipper,"" 夢 (bou, mu, kura.i, yume, yume.miru) meaning ""dream, illusion, vision"" and 武 (bu, mu, take.shi) meaning ""military, warrior.""As a masculine name, it can be used as 亜富, 亜人夢, 亜十夢, 亜登夢, 亜土夢, 阿斗夢, 阿度夢 or 愛斗武 with 人 (jin, nin, -to, hito, -ri) meaning ""person,"" 十 (ji', juu, ju', to, too) meaning ""ten,"" 登 (shou, chou, to, tou, dou, a.garu, nobo.ru) meaning ""ascend, climb up,"" 阿 (a, o, omone.ru, kuma) meaning ""corner, flatter, nook,"" 度 (taku, to, do, -ta.i, tabi) meaning ""degrees, time"" and 土 (to, do, tsuchi) meaning ""earth, ground, soil.""Bearers of this name include footballers Atomu Nabeta (鍋田 亜人夢) (1991-) & Atomu Tanaka (田中 亜土夢) (1987-) and actor Atomu Shimojō (下條 アトム) (1946-).This name is rarely given to children, if given at all."
