Atototl,,,Nahuatl,,,,,,,,"Means ""water bird"" in Nahuatl, from atl ""water"" and tototl ""bird"". Can refer to several specific kinds of birds, including pelicans, herons, wild geese, and other water-dwelling birds."
Atotoztli,f,,Nahuatl|Aztec,/a.to.ˈto.stɬi/(Classical Nahuatl),,,,,,,"Means ""water parrot"", deriving from the Nahuatl elements atl (""water, a body of water"") and toztli (""yellow parrot""). Name borne by an Aztec queen that possibly ruled as tlatoani (ruler of a city-state) in her own right."
