Atthis,f,Ἀτθίς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""Attica"" or ""woman of Attica"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek myth, this was the name of a daughter of King Cranaus, who supposedly named Attica in her honour after she died young."
