Atzimba,f,,"Theatre|Spanish (Mexican, Rare)|Purépecha (?)",/a.ˈtsim.ba/(Mexican Spanish),,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. It appears in Ricardo Castro's tragic opera Atzimba (1900), about a beautiful Purépecha princess who falls in love with the Spanish captain Jorge de Villadiego, an emissary of Hernán Cortés. The story, which is set during the Spanish conquest of Michoacán, Mexico, around 1522 and ends in her suicide, was adapted from a Purépecha legend collected by Eduardo Ruiz and published in Michoacán: Paisajes, Tradiciones y Leyendas (1891). Along with Eréndira and Tzetzangari, Atzimba is one of the three Purépecha princesses represented in the 'Fuente de las Tarascas' monument in Morelia, Michoacán."
