Aurigena,,,Roman Mythology,aw-RIJ-ə-nə,,,,,,,"Means ""born of gold"", derived from Latin aurum ""gold"" and -gena ""born from, sprung from"". This was originally a poetic epithet applied to the legendary hero Perseus (whose father, the god Jupiter, came upon his mother Danaë in the form of a shower of gold). Compare the Greek adjective χρυσόπατρος (chrysopatros) meaning ""sprung of a golden father""; also compare Chrysogonos."
