Avianca,f,,Various (Rare),,,,,,,,"First occurred in the United States Social Security Administration public name dataset in 1990 (when 18 baby girls were given this name), following the Avianca Flight 203 bombing on November 27, 1989, which received widespread media coverage. The name of the Colombian airline Avianca is an acronym of Spanish (A)ero(vía)s (N)acionales de (C)olombi(a) meaning ""National Airways of Colombia"".A known bearer is South African-born former beauty pageant titleholder Avianca Böhm (1990-), who was crowned Miss Universe New Zealand 2012 but was stripped of her crown because she did not hold New Zealand citizenship."
