Aybak,m,,Medieval Turkic,[AHY-bahk]|[AHY-bek],,,,,,,"Aybak is a classical Turkic name formed by the elements Ay (""moon"", representing radiance and celestial grace) and Beg (or Bek, denoting ""ruler"", ""lord"", or ""nobleman""). The combination signifies ""The Moon Lord"" or ""Radiant Nobleman,"" embodying the reflective calm of the moon paired with the authority of the nobility.Widely documented in the 13th-century Mamluk Sultanate; the most prominent figure is Izz ad-Din Aybak, the first Mamluk Sultan of Egypt."
