Ayçelen,f,,Turkish,[ai-CHEH-lehn],,,,,,,"Ayçelen is a modern, evocative Turkish name blending two distinct natural images: Ay (the Moon) and Çelen (a crown, a garland of flowers, or a brilliant crest).The name translates to ""The Lunar Crown"" or ""The Garland of Moonbeams."" In a modern naming context, it represents a child of striking, radiant beauty who wears the light of the moon like royalty. It carries an aura of natural elegance, suggesting a personality that is both artistic and sophisticated, bringing a crowning glory and a soft, luminous peace to her surroundings."
