Aylima,f,Айлыма(Karakalpak Cyrillic),"Karakalpak (Modern, Rare)",[ɑj.li.ˈmɑ],,,,,,,"A lyrical Karakalpak name formed by Ay (""Moon"") and the possessive/attributive suffix -lı/-lıma (""having,"" ""possessing,"" or ""of the moon""). It translates to ""Moon-like,"" ""Of the Moon,"" or ""Moon-bearing."" It evokes a sense of lunar grace and completeness. It signifies a person who possesses the tranquil power of the moon, serving as a beacon of serenity and feminine wisdom within the community."
