Azan,m,"Ἀζᾶν, Ἀζάν(Ancient Greek)|اذان(Urdu)",Greek Mythology|Malay|Indonesian|Urdu,"/ˈa.zan/(Malay, Indonesian)",,,,,,,"Means ""Azanian, of Azania"" in Ancient Greek, Azania being the name of an ancient subregion of Arcadia possibly derived from Ζάν (Zan), a Doric Greek form of Zeus. In Greek mythology, Azan was the eponymous founder of Azania and a son of King Arcas. It was also the name of the husband of Hippolyte."
