Azim,m,"عظيم(Arabic)|Азим(Uzbek, Tajik)|عظیم(Persian)|আজিম(Bengali)",Arabic|Uzbek|Tajik|Persian|Bengali|Malay|Azerbaijani,/ʕa.ˈðˤiːm/(Arabic)|/ʔä.ˈzim/(Tajik Persian)|/ʔæ.ˈziːm/(Persian)|/ˈa.d͡zim/(Bengali)|/ˈa.d͡ʒim/(Bengali)|/æ.ˈzim/(Azerbaijani),,,,,,,"Means ""magnificent, great, supreme, powerful"" in Arabic, a derivative of عظم (ʿaẓuma) meaning ""to be great"". In Islamic tradition العظيم (al-ʿAẓīm) is one of the 99 names of Allah."
