Babürşah,m,,Turkish,/baː.byr.ʃɑh/,,,,,,,"Babür, combined with a Perso-Turkic royal title, şah meaning ""shah"". As a whole, it means ""shah as strong as a tiger"". This was the nickname of Zahir ud-Din Muhammad, the 16th-century founder of the Mughal Empire in India."
