Baderic,m,,Germanic|History,,,,,,,,"Means ""powerful battle"", derived from the Germanic elements badu ""battle"" and rîcja ""powerful, strong, mighty."" The second element is also closely related to Celtic rîg or rix and Gothic reiks, which all mean ""king, ruler."" Baderic was a 6th-century co-king of the Thuringii, a Germanic tribe."
