Bael,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Probably from the name of the Canaanite deity Ba'al. This is the name of a demon who appears in several works on demonology, including the 17th-century grimoire The Lesser Key of Solomon (author unknown), the Pseudomonarchia Daemonum (1563) by Dutch physician Johann Weyer and the Dictionnaire Infernal (1818) by French occultist Jacques Collin de Plancy. He is described as bearing the head of a man, a cat and a toad."
