Bakur,m,Բակուր(Armenian)|ბაკურ(Georgian),Armenian (Rare)|Georgian,[bɑ.ˈkuɾ](Eastern Armenian)|[pʰɑ.ˈɡuɾ](Western Armenian),,,,,,,"Armenian and Georgian form of Pakur. Some of the earliest known bearers of this name are the 2nd-century kings Bakur of Armenia and Bakur of Lazica (in Colchis), who are both better known under the Latin name Pacorus. Other notable bearers include three kings of Caucasian Iberia, each of whom are better known under Bacurius, the latinized form of their name."
