Bartautas,m,,Lithuanian,bahr-TOW-tahs,,,,,,,"An old Lithuanian masculine name composed of two elements: bart meaning ""to scold"", ""to reprimand"", or possibly from barti (verb ""to chide""), and autas, a common masculine name suffix in Baltic compounds. Though the exact historical usage is uncertain, the name may have once conveyed a meaning such as ""he who reprimands"", possibly implying a person of authority, wisdom, or moral judgement. Like many compound names in the Baltic tradition, Bartautas reflects action or traits and may have roots in pre-Christian naming practices."
