Baucis,f,Βαυκίς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek βαυκός (baukos) meaning ""delicate, soft; prudish, disdainful, affected"". In Greek mythology, Baucis and Philemon were an elderly couple who showed great hospitality to the god Zeus. Baucis was also the name of a Greek poet contemporaneous with Sappho and Erinna whose work is now lost, apostrophized in Erinna's 'Distaff'."
