Beadufriþ,m,,Anglo-Saxon,/ˈbæ͜ɑ.du.ˌfriθ/(Old English),,,,,,,"Derived from the Old English elements beadu ""battle"" and friþ ""peace"". Cognate to Old Norse Bárðr."
Beaduheard,m,,Anglo-Saxon,"/ˈbæ͜ɑ.du,xæ͜ɑrd/(Old English)",,,,,,,"Derived from the Old English elements beadu ""battle, war"" and heard ""hard, firm, brave""."
