Befana,f,,Folklore,[Bef-ɛ-na#],,,,,,,"This name belongs to a witch from the Italian Folklore. It is said that Befana is an elderly woman in a flying broom, very similar to a witch. She visits children during the night from 5 to 6 of January, the Epiphany night. Befana gives candy, fruits or small toys to kids who behave well, and pieces of coal to bad-behaving kids. Popular beliefs say the name comes from the Epiphany, however, evidences suggest that Befana has roots in the pagan goddess Strenia."
