Belarmino,m,,Spanish|Galician|Portuguese,,,,,,,,"Spanish, Galician and Portuguese form of Bellarmino, the original Italian surname of Saint Roberto Bellarmine (1542-1621), a cardinal who is regarded as a Doctor of the Church. His surname meant ""well-armed"" from Italian."
