Belaset,f,,Judeo-Anglo-Norman,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old French bele, the feminine form of the adjective biau, bel ""graceful, elegant, courteous; noble; handsome; beautiful"" and Old French assez ""enough; sufficiently"" (which in the context of this name would have been understood as ""very"")."
