Beliña,f,,Galician,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Isabel.
Belina,f,,Gascon|Italian|Albanian|Judeo-Anglo-Norman,,,,,,,,"Gascon diminutive of Isabèl. Belina (known as Béline in French, died 1153) was a Roman Catholic virgin martyr who was canonized by Pope Innocent III in 1203. Due to the saint, this name also saw some usage in Italy. However, in Italy it is also occasionally considered a feminine form of Belenus, hiding behind a Christian guise."
Belindah,f,,"English (African, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Belinda.
Belindia,f,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Elaboration of Belinda.
Béline,f,,French (Rare)|Literature|Theatre|History,,,,,,,,"Gallicized form of Belina. It was used by Molière in his play 'The Imaginary Invalid' (1673) ('Le Malade imaginaire' in French), where it belongs to the wife of Argan."
Beline,f,,English,BEL-EEN,,,,,,,English variant of Béline.
