Bellabeth,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,Combination of Bella and Beth.
Bellabona,f,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin bella meaning ""beautiful, charming, pleasant"" and Latin bona ""good, kind, right, pleasant; valid, useful, healthy"".For the same elements in the reversed order, see Bonabella."
Bellacara,f,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"From Latin bella ""beautiful"" and cara ""dear, beloved"". See also Carabella, which is composed of the same elements in reverse order."
Belladama,f,,Sicilian|Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"From Italian ""bella"" and ""dama"", meaning beautiful lady. Used in Sicily as a variant of Belladonna."
