Belvina,f,,Literature|French (African),bel-VEE-nə,,,,,,,"Apparently from the Latin word meaning ""beast-like"" (also written beluina), derived from bēlua ""beast, monster"" (Italian belva) with the adjectival suffix‎ -īnus ""of, like"". The author J. K. Rowling used this name in her 'Harry Potter' books for a member of the Black family."
