Benchakanlayani,f,เบญจกัลยาณี(Thai),Thai (Rare),/ben˧.t͡ɕa˨˩.kan˧.la˦˥.jaː˧.ˈniː˧/,,,,,,,"Means ""woman of fivefold beauty"" in Thai, from เบญจ (bencha) meaning ""five, fivefold"" and กัลยาณี (kanlayani) meaning ""beautiful girl, belle"". In Buddhism this term refers to a woman with five favourable attributes: beautiful hair, beautiful teeth, beautiful flesh, beautiful skin and beauty at any age."
