Beornhæþ,m,,Anglo-Saxon,/be͜orn.xæːθ/(Old English),,,,,,,"Derived from the Old English elements beorn ""warrior, man"" and hæþ ""heath, wilderness"". This name was borne by an Anglo-Saxon nobleman in Northumbria in the reign of King Ecgfrith (ruled 671–685)."
