Berechiah,m,בֶּרֶכיָהוּ(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,/bɛ.rə.ˈkaɪ.ə/(Biblical English),,,,,,,"Means ""blessing of Yahweh"" in Hebrew, derived from בְּרָכָה (b'rakhá) meaning ""blessing, congratulation"" and יָהּ (yah) referring to the Hebrew God. In the Old Testament, this was the name of several characters, including the father of the Hebrew prophet Zechariah and the son of Zerubbabel."
