Betzy,f,,Spanish (Latin American)|American (Hispanic)|Norwegian,,,,,,,,"Variant of the English name Betsy. Also compare Bethzy. Notable bearers include Betzy Kjelsberg (1866-1950), a Norwegian women's rights activist, suffragist and politician whose mother was from Scotland, and mathematician Mary Ann Elizabeth 'Betzy' Stephansen (1872-1961), the first Norwegian woman to be awarded a doctorate degree."
Beuckel,m,,West Frisian (Archaic)|Medieval Dutch,,,,,,,,"Medieval Frisian diminutive of Beuwe.Medieval Dutch bearers of the name were mostly located in what are now the provinces of North Holland, South Holland and Utrecht. For them, the name might possibly have had a different etymology, in which case a relation with modern Dutch beuk meaning ""beech tree"" seems to be a possibility."
