Bhaavni,f,भानवी(Sanskrit),Hinduism,Bhavānī,,,,,,,"Bhavānī (also known as Bhāvya, Tulajā, Turajā, Tvarita, Aṃbā, Jagadambā and Aṃbē) is an epithet associated with Durga. Bhavani translates to ""giver of life"" Bhavani is a name of Indian origin, deeply rooted in Hindu culture and mythology. It translates to ""the Divine Mother"" or ""the Goddess"", signifying power, fertility, and creation. Primarily used for girls, Bhavani is a name that resonates with strength and spiritual connection."
Bhabani,,"ভবানী(Bengali, Assamese)|ଭବାନୀ(Odia)",Bengali|Odia|Assamese,/ˈbʱɔ.ba.ni/(Bengali)|/bʱɔ.ˈba.n̪i/(Odia),,,,,,,"Bengali, Odia and Assamese form of Bhavani."
