Bhanu,,"भानु(Hindi)|ভানু(Bengali, Assamese)|ଭାନୁ(Odia)|భాను(Telugu)|ಭಾನು(Kannada)|ഭാനു(Malayalam)|பானு(Tamil)",Hindi|Bengali|Assamese|Odia|Telugu|Kannada|Malayalam|Tamil,"/ˈbʱɑː.nʊ/(Hindi)|/ˈbʱa.nu/(Bengali, Assamese)|/ˈbʱa.n̪u/(Odia)|/ˈbʱaː.nu/(Telugu, Malayalam)|/ˈbʰɑː.n̪u/(Kannada)|/ˈbaː.nu/(Malayalam)",,,,,,,"From Sanskrit भानु (bhānu) meaning ""ray of light, brightness, splendour, sun""."
Bhanul,m,भानुल(Hindi),Indian,bhA-nool|bhaanu-l,,,,,,,"Name- Bhanul भानुलMEANING - given by sun, gifted by sun, shining . Here भानु means sun, radiance, shining + ल from word ( ला ) means having or givenOrigin- Sanskrit, Indian, Tamil, Sikh, Buddhist, Nepali, Sinhala"
Bhanumati,f,भानुमती(Hindi),Indian,,,,,,,,"Means ""luminous"" or ""shining like the sun"", from Sanskrit भानु (bhanu) ""ray of light, splendour, brightness; the sun; beautiful woman"" and -मत् (-mat) ""as, like, having the qualities of""."
Bhanupriya,f,भानुप्रिया(Hindi),Hindi,,,,,,,,Derived from Bhanu and Priya.
