Birtvel,m,ბირთველ(Georgian),Georgian (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Derived from Georgian ბირთვისელი (birtviseli) meaning ""of Birtvisi"". Birtvisi is the name of a medieval Georgian fortress, which in medieval Georgia was famous for being impregnable. The fortress likely got its name from ბირთვის (birtvis), the genitive of the Georgian noun ბირთვი (birtvi) meaning ""ball, sphere"" as well as ""kernel, core, nucleus"" (of atom, cell and society)."
