Blade,m,,English|Popular Culture|German (East Prussian),BLAH-deh(East Prussian German),,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Blade or from the Old English blæd ‘leaf of a plant,' of Germanic origin; related to Dutch blad and German Blatt.Blade is the 'hero' name of Marvel comics half-vampire, vampire-hunter, protagonist Eric Brooks. He was portrayed by actor Wesley Snipes in the 'Blade' film trilogy and Kirk ""Sticky Fingaz"" Jones in the television adaptation."
Bladen,m,,"English (American, Rare)",BLAY-dən(American English),,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Bladen. Has resurged in modern terms because of the popular sounds found in other names such as Blade and Braden.
