Bloeme,f,,Dutch (Rare)|Yiddish (Dutchified),BLOO-mə(Dutch),,,,,,,"As a Dutch name, it is a variant of Bloem. But as a Yiddish name, it is a transcription of Blume. A known bearer of this name was Bloeme Evers-Emden (1926-2016), a Dutch Jewish teacher, child psychologist, and author who attended school with the famous diarist Anne Frank (1929-1945)."
