Bolkan,m,,Turkish (Rare),bawl-KAHN [key],,,,,,,"Derived from the Turkish elements bol meaning ""abundant, plentiful"" and kan meaning ""blood"". The name traditionally implies a brave, vigorous, or high-spirited person full of life and vitality (literally ""one with abundant blood"").While it bears a phonetic resemblance to the Turkish word ""Balkan"" (""chain of wooded mountains"") and the Turkish word ""Volkan"" (meaning ""volcano"", itself a loanword from French volcan), these are etymologically unrelated."
