Boram,,"보람(Korean Hangul)|寳濫, 寳蘫, 寳覽, 保濫, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/po̞.ɾäm/,,,,,,,"From native Korean 보람 (boram) meaning ""fruitful, useful, worthwhile.""It can also be written with hanja, such as 寳 (bo) meaning ""treasure"" or 保 (bo) meaning ""protection, defence,"" combining that with 濫 (ram) meaning ""overflow; diffusion; float,"" 蘫 (ram) meaning ""clear water,"" 覽 (ram) meaning ""view; observation; prospect,"" and the such.Female bearers of this name include singer and actress Jeon Boram (1986-) and singer Park Bo-ram (1994-)."
