Borna,m,برنا(Persian),Persian,/ˈbɔːr.nɑː/,,,,,,,"meaning in Persian: Young, Youth, Fresh, Healthy, BraveThe oldest references to the word in Persian literature that I found online were from several poets from Ferdowsi, a great Persian poet from 1000 years ago. the most famous among his poem that all Iranian children learn at elementary school is this:توانا بود هرکه دانا بودز دانش دل پیر برنا بودtranslation;whoever has wisdom, will be powerfulwith wisdom, even an old heart/soul will become Young"
