Borysthenes,m,Βορυσθένης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/bə.ˈrɪs.θən.iːz/(English),,,,,,,"Hellenised form of Proto-Scythian *Baurēštana, derived from *baurēšta ""dark brown"", superlative of *baura ""brown, red, dun"", and the nominal suffix *-na. Possibly influenced by the Ancient Greek word σθένος (sthenos) ""vigour, strength"". In Greek mythology, Borysthenes was the eponymous god of what is now known as the Dnieper river."
