Bozçin,f,,Turkish,[Boz-chin],,,,,,,"A composition of Boz (""grey,"" ""wild,"" ""earth-colored"") and the suffix -çin (often denoting animal or creature types, such as a mountain deer or a wild beast of the steppes). It symbolizes ""the wild spirit of the grey plains,"" representing the untamed, natural majesty of the high plateaus."
