Brandis,f,,American (Modern)|Arthurian Cycle,BRAN-dis,,,,,,,"Apparently a modern invented name, blending Brandy with Candice (or Beatrice), though it coincides with a surname which was taken from a place name (either ""from from a former Brandis castle in Emmental near Bern, Switzerland, or from any of the places so named in Saxony, Germany"", or from the Czech town of Brandýs, on the Labe (Elbe) river (German Brandeis))."
