Brimar,m,,Icelandic,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Old Norse brim meaning ""surf, surge"" (compare Brimir) combined with herr meaning ""army, warrior"". This is also the Icelandic name for the city of Bremen, Germany."
Brimarlo,m,,Spanish,,,,,,,,Not available.
Brimesent,f,,Arthurian Cycle|Literature,,,,,,,,"The name can be interpreted as a dithematic Germanic name composed of brem ""famous; boasting"" and sind ""path, journey"".Arthur’s sister in the Vulgate Merlin.The daughter of Hoel and Igerne (Igraine), she married King Urien (Uriens) and had a son named Yvain (Ywaine). Her sister was called Blasine. She encouraged her son to take service with Arthur.Her role is assumed by Morgan le Fay in the Post-Vulgate."
Brimhildur,f,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Norse elements brim ""surf, surge; surface of the sea"" and hildr ""battle, fight""."
