Buckminster,m,,English (American),,,,,,,,"Transferred use from the placename Buckminster in England.It is the second name of the American architect and inventor Richard Buckminster Fuller, usually known as Buckminster Fuller."
Buckner,m,,American (South),,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Buckner.
Bucky,m,,Popular Culture|American,BUK-ee,,,,,,,"Diminutive of Buck, Buckminster, or Buchanan.It is also the name of Captain America’s best friend Bucky who’s real name was James Buchanan Barnes."
Bucolion,m,,Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Boukolion. This was the name of several characters in Greek mythology, one of them being a king of Arcadia."
Bucolus,m,,Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Boukolos. This is the name of several characters in Greek mythology, one of them being the son of Hippocoön, a king of Sparta."
Bucumi,f,,Rundi,,,,,,,,"Means ""tenth child"" in Kirundi."
Bucur,m,,Medieval Romanian|Romanian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from either Romanian bucur, an archaic form of the adjective bucuros ""joyful"", a bucura ""to become joyful"" or bucurie ""joy"". This name was borne by Bucur, the legendary Romanian shepherd who is said to have founded Bucharest (Bucureşti in Romanian), giving it his name."
Bucura,f,,Medieval Romanian,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Bucur.
Bud,,Буд(Mongolian Cyrillic)|ᠪᠣᠳ᠋(Traditional Mongolian),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Means ""Mercury (planet)"" in Mongolian, ultimately derived from Sanskrit बुध् (budh) meaning ""awaking, intelligent, wise""."
Buda,m,Буда(Buryat Cyrillic),"Hungarian (Rare, Archaic)|Buryat",BOO-daw,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""swelling one (of rounded shapes)"", ""elevated"". This is the Hungarian form of Bleda, the name of the brother of Attila."
Budaq,m,,Azerbaijani,/bu.ˈdɑχ/,,,,,,,"Means ""branch, twig"" in Azerbaijani."
Budashiri,f,ᠪᠦᠳᠬᠠᠱᠢᠷᠢ(Traditional Mongolian)|寶塔實里(Chinese)|보탑실리(Korean Hangul),Medieval Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Etymology unknown, possibly from the Sanskrit 'Buddhashri' meaning ""sacred as a Buddha"". This was the personal name of Princess Supreme Noguk."
Budd,m,,English (American),BUD(American English),,,,,,,"Short form of Buddy. In American culture Bud, Budd, and Buddy were often as a nickname for a son named for his father to avoid name confusion. It later became used as an independent name."
Budda,m,Будда(Mongolian Cyrillic)|ᠪᠤᠳ᠋ᠳ᠋ᠾᠠ(Traditional Mongolian)|仏陀(Japanese Kanji)|ぶっだ(Japanese Hiragana),Anglo-Saxon|Buddhism,/ˈpʊt͉.ta/(Mongolian)|/bɯᵝd̚.dä/(Japanese),,,,,,,"Old English name of uncertain meaning, perhaps related to Brythonic boud ""victory"". It coincides with an Old English word meaning ""beetle"" (and could be a byname derived from it)."
Buddas,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Buddha, borrowed from Ancient Greek Βούδδας (Boúddas) ""Buddha"". This was the renaming of Terebinthus of Turbo, a purported pupil of Scythianus during the 1st to 2nd century AD."
Buddhika,m,බුද්ධික(Sinhala),Sinhalese,,,,,,,,"Means ""reasonable"" in Sinhalese, ultimately from Sanskrit बुद्धि (buddhi)."
Buddhish,m,"बुद्धीश(Sanskrit, Hindi, Marathi, Nepali)",Sanskrit|Hindi|Indian|Hinduism|Tamil|Telugu|Kannada|Malayalam|Bengali|Gujarati|Assamese|Nepali,buddhIsh(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"""lord of wisdom "" ; ""lord of intelligence "". Here बुद्धि means wisdom + ईश means lord"
Buddi,m,,"English (American, Modern)",buh-dee(American English),,,,,,,A variation of Buddy and Buddie
