Burghar,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Old High German burg meaning ""fortress"". Also compare Gothic bairgan (bergan in Old High German) meaning ""to keep, to save, to preserve"". The second element of this name is derived from Old High German hari meaning ""army""."
