Caeculus,m,,Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Latin adjective caecus meaning ""blind"" combined with the Latin masculine diminutive suffix -ulus. Also compare the related name Caecilius.In Roman mythology, Caeculus was the son of the fire god Vulcan. Meanwhile in real life, the Roman gens (""clan, family"") Caecilia claimed that Caeculus was their eponymous ancestor."
