Calah,f,,Hebrew,cayla,,,,,,,"Allegedly from Hebrew כַּלָּה (kallah) meaning ""bride"", a word sometimes used as a metaphor for the Sabbath (hence, ""Shabbat bride""), though it is uncertain whether this is truly used as a Jewish name.Considering the submitted pronunciation is ""cayla"", this may be a variant of the Yiddish name Kaila (which was fairly popular in the 19th century among Ashkenazim Jews)."
