Calais,m,Κάλαϊς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κάλαϊς (Kalais), which meant ""turquoise"" or ""chrysolite"" (being the name of ""a precious stone of a greenish blue""). In Greek myth Calais and his twin brother Zetes, together known as the Boreads (being sons of Boreas, god of the north wind), were Argonauts."
