Cəlaliyyə,f,,Azerbaijani,,,,,,,,"From the Azerbaijani cəlal meaning ""lustre""."
Calam,m,,Irish|English,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. Among anglophone bearers from outside Ireland, there might possibly be cases where the name is derived from the surname Calam, which is ultimately of Scottish origin.A known bearer of this name is the English actor Calam Lynch (b. 1994), whose parents are both Irish."
Calamanda,f,,Catalan (Rare)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"From the Latin word calamus meaning ""reed, cane"". This was the name of a possibly legendary Catalan saint who is the patroness of the town of Calaf (Catalonia)."
Calametis,f,Καλάμητις(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly derived from Ancient Greek καλάμη (kalame) meaning ""reed, stalk, straw (of corn, wheat)"". Calametis was one of the fifty daughters of King Thespius in Greek mythology."
