Caliadne,f,Καλιάδνη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/kæl.i.ˈæd.niː/,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Ancient Greek καλός (kalos) meaning ""beautiful, good"" and ἀδνός (adnos) meaning ""holy, pure, chaste"". In Greek mythology this was the name of a naiad of the river Nile in Egypt. She was one of the wives of king Aegyptus, and bore him twelve sons."
