Canisius,m,,Dutch (Rare),,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Canisius. From the Dutch surname Kanis. Kanis, “covered fish basket” in dialectal Dutch, is the name of an inn that used an upturned fish basket on its signage, it came into usage in honour of the Jesuit and saint Peter Canisius."
