Carneiscus,m,"Καρνεῖσκος, Καρνεΐσκος(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Καρνεῖος (Karneios), an epithet of Apollo referring to the Κάρνεια (Karneia) festival and month, ultimately derived from κάρνος (karnos) meaning ""ram (animal)"". This was the name of an Ancient Greek philosopher of the Epicurean school. His only surviving writing is on the subject of the death of a friend."
