Carnus,m,Κάρνος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""ram (animal)"" in Ancient Greek. This was the name of a seer from Acarnania in Greek mythology, in some accounts a son of Zeus and Europa. He was taught divination by the god Apollo, who took the epithet Carneus and established the Carneia festival after Carnus was killed. Carnus may have originally been an old Peloponnesian agricultural deity later identified with Apollo."
