Castianeira,f,Καστιάνειρα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek κέκασμαι (kekasmai) meaning ""to excel, surpass; to shine"" and ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man"", making this name a doublet of Cassandra. This was the name of a wife or concubine of King Priam in Greek mythology, the mother by him of Gorgythion."
