Catootje,f,,Dutch (Rare)|Literature|Popular Culture,kah-TO-tyə(Dutch),,,,,,,"Diminutive of Cato 2, as it contains the Dutch diminutive suffix -tje. This name is not to be confused with the Dutch noun kadootje meaning ""little present"".In Dutch literature and popular culture, Catootje is the name of the youngest daughter and middle child of the Tromp family from the popular long-running cartoon Jan, Jans en de kinderen (which is known in English as Jack, Jacky and the Juniors). The cartoon was started in 1970 by the Dutch cartoonist Jan Kruis (1933-2017) and is continued to this day by his successors."
Catori,f,,"Obscure|English (American, Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Possibly an invented name, a combination of Catherine and Victoria. Also compare Latori and Natori.Note, many baby name sites and books list this name as meaning 'spirit' in Hopi, but this is incorrect. There is no word for 'spirit' in any Native American language that corresponds to Catori. (Similarly, Kotori is commonly listed as meaning 'screech owl spirit' in Hopi, according to Native Languages of the Americas; they comment: 'Clearly some baby book author made a typo at some point and no one bothered to check it before repeating it, because the Hopi word for screech owl is tokori, not kotori.')"
