Catreus,m,Κατρεύς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˈkeɪ.tri.əs/(English)|/ˈkeɪt.ruːs/(English),,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek κατρεύς (katreus) referring to a kind of bird from India, probably the Himalayan monal pheasant. Alternatively, it could be of pre-Greek origin, perhaps related to κατά (kata) ""downwards, against"". In Greek mythology, this was a king of Crete who was prophesied to be killed by one of his own children, which came to pass when his son mistook him for an attacking pirate from a distance and speared him."
