Caturix,m,,Gaulish|Celtic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Gaulish catu meaning ""battle"" combined with Gaulish rix meaning ""king"".This was the name of the war god of the Helvetii, a Gaulish tribe. He was also important for the Gaulish tribe of the Caturiges, since they named themselves after him. The god eventually became known as Mars Caturix in Gallo-Roman religion through identification with the Roman god Mars."
