Celeborn,m,,Literature,KEL-e-born,,,,,,,"Means ""tree of silver"" or ""tall and silver"" in Sindarin, from the elements celeb ""silver"" and orne ""tree"" or possibly a derivative of ornā meaning ""tall"". In J.R.R. Tolkien's 'The Lord of the Rings', Celeborn was the ruler of Lothlórien along with his wife Galadriel."
