Chakuriya,f,"茶栗夜, 茶栗屋(Japanese Kanji)|ちゃくりや(Japanese Hiragana)|チャクリヤ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),CHYAH-KOO-REE-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 茶 (cha) meaning tea, combined with 栗 (kuri) meaning ""chestnut"", and 夜 (ya, yoru) meaning ""night"" or 屋 (ya) meaning ""shop"". Other kanji or kanji combinations can form this name as well."
