Chaloner,m,,Obscure,,,,,,,,"From the surname Chaloner, a variant of Challinor, itself denoting a blanket maker, from Middle English chaloun ""blanket"". A famous bearer of the name was Admiral of the Fleet Sir Chaloner Ogle (1681-1750) who killed Bartholomew Roberts, who many consider the mark that ended the Golden Age of Piracy."
