Changpu,,"菖蒲, 昌璞, 昌浦, 昌普, 昌谱, 昌蒲, 常浦, 常普, 长璞, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/ʈ͡ʂʰɑŋ.pʰu/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 菖蒲 (chāngpú) meaning ""Acorus"" or ""iris""; or from Chinese 昌 (chāng) meaning ""flourish, prosper, good, sunlight"", 常 (cháng) meaning ""common, frequent, regular"", or 长 (cháng) meaning ""long"" combined with 璞 (pú) meaning ""uncut jade or stone containing jade"", 浦 (pǔ) meaning ""water’s edge, river mouth"", or 普 (pǔ) meaning ""general, universal, common"". Other hanzi combinations are possible."
