Chariklo,f,Χαρικλώ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/xa.ri.ˈklo/(Koine Greek)|/kə.ˈrɪ.kloʊ/(English)|/ˈkæ.rɪ.kloʊ/(English),,,,,,,"Derived from Greek χάρις (charis) meaning ""grace, kindness"" combined with either κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory"" (compare Chariclea) or κλώθω (klotho) meaning ""to spin, to twist by spinning"". This was the name of two different nymphs in Greek mythology, one a close friend of the goddess Athena and mother of the blind seer Teiresias, the other a nymph of Mount Pelion and wife of the centaur Chiron."
