Cheol-yeong,m,"철영(Korean Hangul)|哲英, 哲榮, 哲永, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕʰʌ̹ɭ.jʌŋ/,,,,,,,"From From Sino-Korean 哲 (cheol) meaning ""wise, sage"" combined with 英 (yeong) meaning ""flower, petal, brave, hero"" or 榮 (yeong) meaning ""glory, honour, flourish, prosper"" or 永 (yeong), meaning ""perpetual, eternal"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
