Chigusa,f,"千種, 千草, 智草, 知草, 千久紗, 智久紗(Japanese Kanji)|ちぐ沙(Kanji/Hiragana)|ちぐさ(Japanese Hiragana)|チグサ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,CHEE-GUU-SAH,,,,,,,"This name can be used as 千種, 千草, 智草 or 知草 with 千 (sen, chi) meaning ""thousand,"" 智 (chi) meaning ""intellect, wisdom,"" 知 (chi, shi.raseru, shi.ru) meaning ""know, wisdom,"" 種 (shu, -gusa, tane) meaning ""class, kind, seed, species, variety"" and 草 (sou, kusa, kusa-, -gusa) meaning ""grass, herb, weed.""Examples of Chigusa with 3 kanji include 千久紗 and 智久紗 with 久 (kyuu, ku, hisa.shii) meaning ""long time"" and 紗 (sa, sha, usuginu) meaning ""gauze, gossamer.""Chigusa can also be used by combining 2 phonetic characters (ちぐ) making up Chigu and 沙 (sa, sha, suna, yonageru) meaning ""sand.""As a word, Chigusa (千種 & 千草) refers to a great variety of flowering plants. Also, it's an abbreviation of 千草色 (chigusairo/ちぐさいろ) which resembles a light greenish-blue colour.Chigusa is also used as a surname."
