Chindamani,f,จินดามณี(Thai),Thai,/t͡ɕin˧.daː˧.ma˦˥.ˈniː˧/,,,,,,,"Means ""wishing gem, wishing stone"". From Thai จินดา (chinda) meaning ""precious jewels"" and มณี (mani) meaning ""jewel, gem"". It is also the name of the first Thai textbook written by scholar and poet Phra Horathibodi to compile and organize fundamental language principles of the 17th century."
