Chise,f,"智世, 知世, 茅瀬, 千星(Japanese Kanji)|ちせ(Japanese Hiragana)|チセ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,CHEE-SEH,,,,,,,"From the Japanese kanji 智 or 知 (chi) meaning ""wisdom; knowledge"" combined with 世 (se) meaning ""epoch; generation"". It can also derive from 茅 (chi) meaning ""miscanthus reed"" and 瀬 (se) meaning ""current, rapids"" or 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" with 星 (se) meaning ""star"".Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chisei,,"ちせい(Japanese Hiragana)|チセイ(Japanese Katakana)|治声, 地成, 散世, 薙靖, 茅勢, 千生, 稚聖, 知星, 智性, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-SE,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 星 (sei) meaning ""dot, star"". In vocabulary, 知性 (chisei) means ""intelligence, intellect"" and 治世 (chisei) means ""regime, govern, rule"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Chiseko,f,"千世子, 千勢子, 千征子, 千成子, 千聖子, 知世子, 知是子, 智勢子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-SE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 知 (chi) meaning ""wisdom"" or 智 (chi) meaning ""knowledge, wisdom"", 世 (se) meaning ""generations"", 勢 (se) meaning ""forces, energy, military strength"", 征 (se) meaning ""to go on a long journey"", 成 (se) meaning ""to become"", 聖 (se) meaning ""holy, sacred"" or 是 (se) meaning ""justice, right"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chisela,f,,Aragonese,,,,,,,,Aragonese form of Gisela.
Chishimba,,,Bemba,[chee-SHIM-bah],,,,,,,"The name Chishimba originates from the Bemba people of Zambia, a Bantu-speaking ethnic group. It holds cultural and linguistic significance in Zambia. The name derives from the Bemba language and carries meanings rooted in positivity and charm.Meaning:The name Chishimba means ""charm"" or ""attraction"" and signifies someone with a captivating and warm personality. It describes ""a pleasing personality, manner, or appearance that makes someone captivating or enchanting to others."" In some contexts, it is interpreted as a ""gift from God"" or a reflection of divine favor.It also reflects ""the power of attraction or influence,"" meaning a special ability to win affection, admiration, or attention, often effortlessly. Chishimba embodies qualities such as kindness, grace, and beauty, and it is associated with individuals who bring light and positivity to those around them."
