Chitrangada,m,चित्राङ्गद(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/t͡ɕit̪.ˈɾɑːŋ.ɡɐ.d̪ɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""decorated with brilliant bracelets"" from Sanskrit चित्र (citra) meaning ""bright, clear, excellent"" and अङ्गद (aṅgada) meaning ""bracelet worn on the upper arm, armband"". In the Hindu epic the Mahabharata this is the name of a Chandravamsha (Lunar dynasty) king of Kuru and a son of Shantanu."
