Chiune,m,千畝(Japanese Kanji)|ちうね(Japanese Hiragana)|チウネ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 畝 (une) meaning ""ridge in a field"". A notable bearer of this name was the Japanese diplomat Chiune Sugihara (1900-1986), who helped thousands of Jews flee Europe during World War II. Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
