Chiura,m,千浦(Japanese Kanji)|ちうら(Japanese Hiragana)|チウラ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),CHEE-UU-ṘAH,,,,,,,"This name is used as 千浦 with 千 (sen, chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 浦 (ho, ura) meaning ""inlet, seacoast, seashore.""One bearer of this name was Japanese-American artist Chiura Obata (小圃 千浦) (1885-1975).This name is very rarely given to boys, if given at all.Chiura is also used as a surname."
