Chlore,m,,French,,,,,,,,French form of Chlorus.
Chloreus,m,,Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Chloreus is an effeminate eunuch priest of Cybele in the Aeneid. Camilla attempts to kill him for his armor, and is in turn killed by Arruns."
Chlorice,f,,"English (American, Rare, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Possibly a blend of Chloris and Clarice.
Chlorie,m,,English,,,,,,,,Not available.
Chlorine,f,,"American (South, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Possibly an elaboration of Chloris.
Chlorissa,f,,English (Modern),,,,,,,,"Elaborated form of Chloris, influenced by Clarissa."
Chlorus,m,,Late Roman,,,,,,,,"Latinized form of the Greek word khlôros ""pale green"" (see also Chloris). This name was borne by a Western Roman emperor from the 3rd century AD."
Chlotaire,m,,History (Gallicized),,,,,,,,French form of Chlothar.
Chlotharius,m,,Germanic (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Chlothar.
Chlothild,f,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old High German hlûd ""famous"" combined with Old Norse hildr ""battle."""
Chlothilde,f,,Germanic|History,,,,,,,,"Variant of Chlothild. Chlothilde was the wife of Clovis I, a Merovingian king of the Franks."
Chlothsind,f,,Frankish,,,,,,,,"From the Frankish element hroþi, ""fame, glory"", and Gothic swinþs. Chlothsind was a Frankish princess who became the queen consort of the Lombard king Alboin."
Chmicha,f,,Arabic (Maghrebi),,,,,,,,Not available.
Chẳng,,,Vietnamese,/t͡ɕaŋ˧˩/|/t͡ɕaŋ˧˨/|/caŋ˨˩˦/,,,,,,,"Means ""not at all"" in Vietnamese."
Chngatux̂,,,Aleut,/t͡ʃ.ŋ.a.t.u.χ/,,,,,,,"Ancient Aleut personal name meaning ""Sea otter"""
Chnodomar,m,,Germanic|History,,,,,,,,"Variant spelling of Cnodomar. Chnodomar was the name of a 4th-century king of the Alamanni, a Germanic tribe."
Chnodomarius,m,,Germanic (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Chnodomar.
Cho,,ချော(Burmese)|ချို(Burmese),Burmese|Burmese|Vietnamese (Rare),/t͡ɕʰɔ́/|/t͡ɕʰò/|/t͡ɕɔ˧˧/|/cɔ˧˧/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Burmese ချော (see Chaw).
Chó,,,Vietnamese (Rare),/t͡ɕɔ˧˦/|/t͡ɕɔ˨˩˦/|/cɔ˦˥/,,,,,,,"Means ""dog"" in Vietnamese."
