Chocian,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Chociesław.
Chociebąd,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,Not available.
Chociebor,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Old Church Slavonic xotěti or xŭtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic xъtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"". Also compare modern Czech chtít, modern Polish chcieć and modern Serbo-Croatian hteti, all of which mean ""to want, to wish, to desire"". The second element is derived from Slavic bor ""battle"" or borit ""to fight""."
Chociemir,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Old Church Slavonic xotěti or xŭtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic xъtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"". Also compare modern Czech chtít, modern Polish chcieć and modern Serbo-Croatian hteti, all of which mean ""to want, to wish, to desire"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace""."
Chociesław,m,,Medieval Polish,khaw-CHEH-swaf(Old Polish),,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Old Church Slavonic xotěti or xŭtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic xъtěti ""to want, to wish, to desire"". Also compare modern Czech chtít, modern Polish chcieć and modern Serbo-Croatian hteti, all of which mean ""to want, to wish, to desire"". The second element is derived from Slavic slav ""glory""."
Chòck,m,,Kashubian,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Chòcemir.
Choćka,m,Хоцька(Belarusian),Belarusian (Archaic),/ˈxot͡sʲ.ka/,,,,,,,"Derived from Belarusian хацець (chacieć) meaning ""to want, to desire"". This name was given to a long-desired child."
Chocola,,,Popular Culture,Cho-ko-lə(English)|Sho-ko-lah(French)|Sho-ko-rah(Japanese),,,,,,,"Chocola is the romanization of the French word 'chocolat' which means ""chocolate"".Famous bearers include:Chocola, a character in the manga Neko ParaChocola, a female bear Sweetspet character who debuted in the anime Jewelpet Sunshine Chocola, a character in the anime Yes! Precure 5 GoGo!Chocola, one of the main charcters in the anime Tezuka Osamu no Don DraculaChocola the Chao, a character that appears in Sonic Heroes who is the brother of Cheese the Chao."
Chocolat,f,,Popular Culture,Sho-ko-lah(French)|Sho-ko-rah(Japanese),,,,,,,"'Chocolat' means ""chocolate"" in French.Famous bearers include:Chocolat, a Japanese singer Chocolat Aikawa, the main character in the anime Chocolat no MahouIn the manga and anime Sugar Sugar Rune, there is a female witch character called Chocolat Meilleure (her name romanized as Chocola). Chocolat, main character in the anime Ore no Nounai Sentakushi ga, Gakuen Love Comedy wo Zenryoku de Jama Shiteiru"
Chocoronú,f,,Romani (Caló),cho-ko-ro-NOO(Caló),,,,,,,"Means ""remedy"" in Caló. This name is used as the Caló form of Remedios."
Choden,,ཆོས་ལྡན(Tibetan),Tibetan|Bhutanese,/t͡ɕʰøː˥˨.tɛ̃˩˨/(Tibetan),,,,,,,"From Tibetan ཆོས་ལྡན (chos-ldan) meaning ""devout, righteous, pious""."
Chodijah,f,,Indonesian,,,,,,,,Indonesian variant of Khadija.
Chodofrodo,m,,"Aragonese (Rare, Archaic)",cho-do-FROH-do,,,,,,,Aragonese form of Godfrey.
