Chonghe,,"充和, 崇河, 重河, 崇荷, 重荷, 崇和, 重和, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/ʈ͡ʂʰʊŋ.xɤ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 崇 (chóng) meaning ""esteem, honour, venerate"" or 重 (chóng) meaning ""repeat, duplicate"" combined with 河 (hé) meaning ""river, stream"" or 荷 (hé) meaning ""lotus, waterlilly"" or 和 (hé) meaning ""harmony, peace"". Other hanzi combinations are possible."
Chongheng,m,崇恒(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 崇 (chóng) meaning ""esteem, honor, revere, venerate"" and 恒 (héng) meaning ""constant, regular, persistent""."
Chonghua,,"重华, 崇华(Chinese)|重華(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese|Chinese Mythology,/ʈʂʊŋ.xwa/(Chinese),,,,,,,"From Chinese 重 (chóng) meaning ""repeat, duplicate"" or 崇 (chóng) meaning ""esteem, honor, venerate"" and 华 (huá) meaning ""splendid, illustrious, flowery, Chinese"". Other characters can also form this name.Chonghua (重华) was the supposed personal name of Emperor Shun, one of the Five Emperors said to have ruled in the early days of Chinese civilization. He was especially known as a paragon of filial piety, and was chosen by the preceding ruler, Yao, to be his successor. Ehuang and Nuying were his wives, while Xiaoming and Zhuguang were his daughters."
