Chrys,,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Chris.
Chryša,m,,Sorbian,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Chrystof.
Chrysafios,m,,Greek,,,,,,,,Not available.
Chrysafis,m,Χρυσάφης(Greek),Greek (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Chrysafios.
Chrysalde,m,,Theatre,,,,,,,,"A character in Molière's ""L'école des femmes"" (The School for Wives )."
Chrysale,m,,Theatre,,,,,,,,"Chrysale is a character in the play ""Les Femmes Savantes"" (The Learned Ladies), a comedy by Molière."
Chrysalis,,,English (Rare)|Filipino (Rare),/ˈkɹɪs.ə.lɪs/(English),,,,,,,"From the word referring to the pupa of a butterfly or moth or the cocoon where the pupa is enclosed inside, derived via Latin from Ancient Greek χρυσαλλίς (khrusallís), from χρυσός (khrusós) meaning ""gold.""A My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic villain bears this name."
Chrysander,m,,"Spanish (Philippines, Rare)",,,,,,,,Not available.
