Chthonophyle,f,Χθονοφύλη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek χθών (chthon) meaning ""ground, earth, soil"" (genitive χθονός) and φυλή (phyle) meaning ""tribe, race"". This was the name of a princess of Sicyon in Greek mythology."
Chu,f,"楚, 初, 俶, 处, etc.(Chinese)",Theatre|Chinese|Filipino (Rare)|Vietnamese|Dena'ina,/ʈʂʰu/|/ˈt͡ʃu/|/t͡ɕu˧˧/|/t͡ɕʊw˧˧/|/cʊw˧˧/|/t͡ʃʰu/,,,,,,,Mamma Chu is a character in the play Mummified Deer written by Luis Valdez.
Chú,,主(Chinese),Chinese (Hokkien)|Vietnamese,/t͡suo/(Hokkien)|/t͡sy/(Hokkien)|/t͡su/(Hokkien)|/t͡ɕu˧˦/|/t͡ɕʊw˨˩˦/|/cʊw˦˥/,,,,,,,Hokkien Chinese form of Zhu.
