Çilem,f,,Turkish,[tʃilɛm],,,,,,,"The name Çilem is deeply rooted in the imagery of growth and the gentle touch of nature. It stems from çıl, a root signifying ""spot,"" ""mottled,"" or ""mark,"" often describing the beauty of a partridge's plumage. This is cognate with çal (""mottled""). Furthermore, it draws from the verb çile- (""to wet slightly""), derived from çi (""moisture,"" ""dew""). It acts as a symbol of the morning dew or the delicate, speckled beauty of the natural world; a gentle, cooling touch upon the earth.It is entirely unrelated to the Persian çile/çihil (forty); it is a purely Turkic name denoting natural elegance."
