Cinaedion,f,Κιναίδιον(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κιναιδιον (Kinaidion), which meant ""(Eurasian) Wryneck"", a type of small grey-brown woodpecker (traditionally associated with passionate and restless love as well as witchcraft, i.e., used by witches in a charm to recover unfaithful lovers). In Greek mythology this was an epithet of the nymph Iynx."
