Çınay,f,,Turkish,[tʃɯ.nɑj],,,,,,,"A lyrical compound of Çın (""Truth"") and Ay (""Moon""). It translates to ""The Resonating Moon"" or ""The Moon of Truth."" It paints the image of a light so pure and clear that it illuminates the absolute truth. It represents someone who is both beautiful and deeply authentic, a beacon of clarity in a dark or chaotic world."
