Cisseus,m,Κισσεύς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),/kis.sěu̯s/(Attic Greek)|/cis.ˈseɸs/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""ivy-crowned"" in Ancient Greek, derived from κισσόω (kissoô) meaning ""to wreathe with ivy"", ultimately from κισσός (kissos) ""ivy"". This is the name of several characters in Greek mythology, including one of the fifty sons of King Aegyptus who was killed by his wife, Antheleia, on their wedding night."
