Cleochares,m,Κλεοχάρης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory"" combined with either χαίρω (chairo) meaning ""to be happy, full of cheer; to enjoy"" or the related χάρις (charis) meaning ""grace, kindness""."
Cleocharia,f,Κλεοχαρεία(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κλεοχαρεία (Kleochareia), derived from κλέος (kleos) ""glory"" and χάρις (charis) ""grace, kindness"". In Greek mythology, Cleocharia was a naiad and queen consort. She was the wife of King Lelex of Laconia and the mother of Myles and Polycaon."
