Corceca,f,,Literature|Arthurian Cycle,KAWR-sə-kə,,,,,,,"Means ""blind heart"" or ""blindness of heart"" from Latin cor meaning ""heart"" and caecus meaning ""blind"". In Edmund Spenser's poem The Faerie Queene (1590) this is the name of an old blind woman who practices Catholic rituals and prays the rosary, the mother of Abessa (Superstition), representing blind commitment to ritual and empty prayers."
