Cortes,f,,"Spanish (European, Rare)",/ˈkoɾ.tes/(European Spanish),,,,,,,"From the titles of the Virgin Mary, Nuestra Señora de Cortes and La Virgen de Cortes, meaning ""Our Lady of Cortes"" and ""The Virgin of Cortes"" respectively (coincides with the words meaning ""cut; style, type"" or ""courts"").She is the patroness of Alcaraz in the province of Albacete in central Spain."
