Cranaë,f,Κρανάη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Cranaus, meaning ""stony"" in Ancient Greek. This was the name of an Athenian princess in Greek mythology, the daughter of King Cranaus. It is also the name of an island off the coast of Gytheio, where Paris of Troy and Helen spent their first night together in Greek mythology."
Cranaechme,f,Κραναίχμη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""rocky point"", from Ancient Greek κραναός (kranaos) meaning ""rocky, rugged"" and αἰχμή (aichme) meaning ""point of a spear, head of an arrow"", or figuratively ""war"". In Greek mythology Cranaechme was a daughter of King Cranaus of Athens. Her sisters were Cranaë and Atthis."
Cranaus,m,Κραναός(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek|Late Greek,/ˈkræn.i.əs/(English),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Κραναός (Kranaos), meaning ""rocky, rugged"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, this was the name of the second king of Athens."
