Crassus,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Roman cognomen which was derived from the Latin adjective crassus, which can mean ""solid, thick, dense"" as well as ""fat, gross, plump"". This name was borne by several ancient Romans, such as the Roman general and politician Marcus Licinius Crassus (1st century BC)."
