Creirwy,f,,Welsh|Welsh Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""token of the egg"", and in effect ""mundane egg"", from Welsh creir ""a token, jewel, sacred object"" and wy ""egg"". In the Mabinogion, a collection of tales from Welsh myth, she was a daughter of Ceridwen and one of the three most beautiful maids of the Isle of Britain. This was also the name of a 6th-century Breton saint from Wales."
