Cunedda,m,,Medieval Welsh,,,,,,,,"From Old Welsh Cunedag, from a Brythonic name *Cuno-dagos meaning ""good hound, having good hounds"", derived from Celtic *kū ""dog, hound"" and *dagos ""good"" (whence Welsh da). This was the name of several early Welsh rulers, notably Cunedda ap Edern, a 5th-century king of Gwynedd and the progenitor of the royal dynasty of Gwynedd."
