Cutha,m,,Anglo-Saxon,/ˈkuː.θɑ/(Old English),,,,,,,"A monothematic Old English name deriving from the Old English element cuþ ""known, familiar"". This name is attested as a given name, but can be a diminutive of any name beginning with Cuth-. One notable bearer was a recorded son of Ceawlin of Wessex."
