Cuthred,m,,Anglo-Saxon|History,,,,,,,,"Means ""famous counsel"", derived from Old English cuþ ""known, familiar"" and ræd ""counsel, advice"".Known bearers of this name include king Cuthred of Wessex (8th century AD) and king Cuthred of Kent (early 9th century AD)."
