Cyane,f,Κυανη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κυανη (Kyane) which was derived from κυανος (kyanos) ""cyan, azure-blue"" (compare Cyan). In Greek myth she was the Naiad nymph of a spring in the Sicilian town of Syracuse, who dissolved away into the spring from grief after witnessing Hades' abduction of her playmate Persephone."
