Cymatolege,f,Κυματολήγη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""wave-stiller, calmer of waves"", derived from Ancient Greek κῦμα (kyma) meaning ""wave, billow"" and λήγω (lego) meaning ""to stay, abate, cease"". This was the name of a Nereid, a sea-nymph daughter of Nereus. Alternatively, it may have been another name of Cymopolea."
Cymbaline,f,,"American (Rare, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Variant of Cymbeline.
