Daiyu,,"黛玉, 岱舆, 戴玉, 代玉, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese|Literature,/tai.yː/(Chinese)|/tai.ɥy/(Chinese),,,,,,,"From Chinese 黛 (dài) meaning ""a black pigment used by women in ancient times to paint their eyebrows"" combined with 玉 (yù) meaning ""jade"". Other hanzi combinations are possible. Lin Daiyu (also spelled Lin Tai-yu, Chinese: 林黛玉; pinyin: Lín Dàiyù, rendered Black Jade in Chi-chen Wang's translation) is one of the principal characters of Cao Xueqin's classic 18th-century Chinese novel Dream of the Red Chamber."
