Dajana,f,,German (Modern),dah-YAH-nah|DAH-yah-nah,,,,,,,"Modern German name of disputed origin.Suggested theories include:1.) A phonetic spelling reflecting the English pronunciation of Diana.2.) A variant of Dayana.3.) A modern coinage based on Turkish dayanmak ""to resist"".4.) A modern coinage based on Arabic daya ""foster mother; nurse"".5.) A borrowing of the Croatian and Serbian name Dajana.The name has been used in Germany since the 1960s."
