Damonno,f,Δαμοννώ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|History,,,,,,,,"Derived from δᾶμος (damos), the Doric Greek form of δῆμος (demos) meaning ""the people"", combined with either an abbreviated form of νίκη (nike) ""victory"" (see Demonike) or ὄνη (one) ""help"", from ὀνίνημι (oninemi) ""to help, support, be useful; to delight, please"". Damonno was a possibly legendary queen of Lydia married to King Cadys, who indirectly caused her husband’s death by murdering his doctor, exiled his twin brother Ardys, and installed her lover Spermes on the throne. It’s unknown what happened to her after that, though Spermes was killed two years later and Ardys returned to rule."
