Dares,m,Δάρης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly derived from Ancient Greek δαρείς (dareis) meaning ""the beaten"", a participle of δέρω (dero) meaning ""to skin, flay; to cudgel, thrash"". Dares Phrygius is the name of a Trojan priest of Hephaestus in Homer’s Iliad, later becoming known as the author of a lost eyewitness account of the fall of Troy. It’s also the name of a young Trojan boxer in Virgil’s Aeneid."
