Da-san,m,다산(Korean Hangul),Korean,,,,,,,,"Means ""the mountain of tea"" from Sino-Korean 茶山.A noted bearer is Jeong Yak-yong (1762-1836), most commonly known by his pen name Dasan. He was one of the greatest thinkers of the later Joseon period, wrote highly influential books about philosophy, science and theories of government, held significant administrative positions, was a close confident of King Jeongjo (ruled 1776-1800), and was noted as a poet. His philosophical position is often identified with the Silhak (practical learning) school, his concerns are better seen as explorations of Neo-Confucian themes."
Dasan,m,,Pomo,,,,,,,,"Dasan, the high god-ancestor of the northern Pomo, came out of the ocean and called the world into being with his words and then created the first people.While it's unknown if Dasan was used as a given name historically, it is a name used by the Pomo in present day."
Dasani,,,"African American (Modern, Rare)",/də.ˈsɑː.ni/,,,,,,,"From the name of the bottled water brand Dasani, itself inspired in the Latin word sanus (""healthy""). This name was first recorded in the US in 1999, the year the brand was launched."
