Datavahya,m,,Old Persian,,,,,,,,"Means ""born better"" or ""created better"", from Old Persian 𐎭𐎠𐎫 (data) meaning ""given, created; born"" and 𐎺𐏃𐎹𐏀 (vahyaz) ""better"", a comparative form of 𐎺𐎢 (vahu) ""good""."
Datbyeol,,닻별(Korean Hangul),"Korean (Modern, Rare)",/tät̚.p͈jʌɭ/,,,,,,,"From native Korean 닻별 (datbyeol), referring to the Cassiopeia constellation, from a combination of 닻 (dat) meaning ""anchor"" and Byeol.The weekend comedy drama series 'Dummy Mommy' (바보엄마 (Babo Eomma)), which features a young girl with this name, led to a temporary increase of the name's usage in 2012."
