Dedisimedi,f,დედისიმედი(Georgian),Georgian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Means ""mother's hope"" in Georgian. It is derived from Georgian დედის (dedis) meaning ""of the mother"" combined with the Georgian noun იმედი (imedi) meaning ""hope"" (see Imeda).This name was borne by a 16th-century princess consort of Samtskhe."
Dedol,m,,Medieval English,,,,,,,,Not available.
Dedomir,m,,Medieval Slavic,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is probably derived from Old Church Slavonic dědŭ ""grandfather"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic dědъ ""grandfather"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". As such, the meaning of this name would roughly be ""grandfather of peace""."
