Deiphontes,m,Δηϊφόντης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/diː.ɪ.ˈfɒn.tiːz/(English),,,,,,,"Probably derived from Ancient Greek δάϊος (daios) meaning ""hostile, destructive, burning"" and the suffix φόντης (phontes) meaning ""slayer of"" (see φόνος (phonos) ""murder, slaughter""). This was the name of a king of Argos in Greek mythology."
