Dekabrin,m,Декабрин(Russian),Soviet|Russian,/dʲɪ.kɐ.ˈbrʲin/(Russian),,,,,,,"Derived from Russian декабрь (dekabr) meaning ""December"". This name was created by Communist parents who were eager to reject traditional names, and was used in order to commemorate the Decembrist revolt of 1825. Also compare the related name Dekabrist."
