Demoleon,m,Δημολέων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/dɛː.mo.lé.ɔːn/(Attic Greek)|/ði.mo.ˈle.on/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""lion of the people"", derived from Greek δῆμος (demos) meaning ""the people"" and λέων (leon) meaning ""lion"". This is the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including both a Trojan and a Greek warrior, and a centaur who fought in the battle against the Lapiths."
