Derkje,,,Dutch|West Frisian,,,,,,,,"When borne by a female person, this name is a good example of how one can turn a very masculine name (Derk) into a feminine name by simply adding the diminutive suffix je to the original name. But when borne by a male person, this name is simply a pet form because of the diminutive suffix."
Derkylidas,m,Δερκυλίδας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Derkylos"" in Greek, derived from the name Derkylos combined with ίδας (idas), which is the Aeolic and Doric Greek form of the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).This name was borne by a Spartan commander from the 4th century BC. He is better known under the latinized form of his name, which is Dercylidas."
