Dexamene,f,Δεξαμένη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""reservoir, tank, receptacle"" or ""one who receives, one who is receptive"", derived from Greek δέχομαι (dekhomai) meaning ""to receive, accept"". This is the name of one of the Nereids."
Dexamenus,m,"Δεξάμενος, Δεξαμενός(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),/dɛk.ˈsæ.mɪn.əs/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""receiving, accepting, welcoming"" in Ancient Greek, a participle of δέχομαι (dekhomai) ""to receive, accept"". This is the name of several characters in Greek mythology."
