Dhumavati,f,धूमावती(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/d̪ʱuː.ˈmɑː.ʋɐ.t̪iː/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""resembling smoke, smokey"" from Sanskrit धूम (dhūma) meaning ""smoke, vapour, mist"" combined with the suffix वती (vatī) meaning ""resemblance, having"". Dhumavati is the seventh of the nine Mahavidyas, the Tantric manifestations of the Hindu mother goddess Mahadevi. She is depicted as an old widow with smokey dark skin sitting atop a chariot and holding a winnowing basket in one hand."
