Dolma,f,སྒྲོལ་མ(Tibetan),Tibetan|Bhutanese|Buddhism,,,,,,,,"From Tibetan སྒྲོལ་མ (sgrol-ma) meaning ""saviouress"" (referring to enlightenment), derived from སྒྲོལ (sgrol) meaning ""to liberate, to save"" and the feminine particle མ (ma). This is the Tibetan name for the bodhisattva Tara."
Dolo,f,,Catalan,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Dolors.
Dolola,f,,English (American),də-LO-LA(American English),,,,,,,"Variant of Dolores, influenced by its nickname Lola"
Dolon,m,Δόλων(Ancient Greek)|দোলন(Bengali),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek|Bengali|Arthurian Cycle,Dōlana,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek δόλος (dolos), which literally means ""bait"" and has a figurative meaning of ""deceit, guile, treachery, trickery"" (see Dolos). Coincides with δόλων (dolon) meaning ""secret weapon, poniard, stiletto knife"". In Greek mythology, Dolon was a Trojan spy known for his swiftness, who was captured and killed by the Greeks after being interrogated."
Dolopion,m,Δολοπίων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the given name Δόλοψ (Dolops), which could derive from the Ancient Greek tribe of the Dolopes, or else directly from δολοπεύω (dolopeuo) meaning ""to plot, scheme"" (related to Dolos). In Greek mythology, Dolopion was a Trojan priest and father of Hypsenor."
Dolops,m,Δόλοψ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˈðo.lops/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Possibly derived from the name of the Dolopes tribe, or perhaps from Ancient Greek δόλοψ (dolops) meaning ""spy, lurker in ambush"", itself related to δόλος (dolos) ""bait, trap; trick, deceit"". Compare Dolopion. This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including a son of Hermes, a brother of Chiron, and two Trojan warriors."
