Doori,m,通(Japanese Kanji)|どおり(Japanese Hiragana)|ドオリ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),DO:-ṘEE,,,,,,,"This name is used as 通 (tsu, tsuu, kayo.u, too.shi, too.su, too.ri, -too.ri, too.ru, -doo.shi, -doo.ri) meaning ""avenue, commute, pass through, traffic.""One bearer of this name is actor and singer Dōri Sakurada (桜田 通) (1991-).The number of people named Dōri is quite low. Usually, most people who are given the kanji for Dōri are named Tōru."
Doorke,,,Limburgish,DAWR-kə|DO:R-kə,,,,,,,"Limburgish diminutive form of Door. Although seen on both genders, it is most often used on females."
Doornroosje,f,,Folklore|Literature,/ˌdoːrn.ˈroːs.jə/,,,,,,,"Dutch calque of Dornröschen. It consists of the Dutch words doorn meaning ""thorn"" and roos meaning ""rose"" combined with the Dutch diminutive suffix -je."
