Dorimedont,m,,"Russian (Rare, Archaic)|Romanian (Rare, Archaic)",DOH-REE-MEH-DONT(Russian),,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek Δορυμέδοντος, means ""master of spear"", where δόρυ=""spear"" and μέδων, μέδοντος=""master, chief"". While this name has been exceedingly rare even in Russian Empire, in Soviet era and modern Russia it seems already extinct."
