Doroftei,m,,Romanian,,,,,,,,"Romanian male name, primarily used as a surname, but also originating from a given name. Derives from the Greek name Dorotheos (Δωρόθεος). It is a combination of the Greek words ""doron"" (gift) and ""theos"" (god), translating to ""gift of God"". It is the equivalent of the Latin name Deodatus or the Slavic-based Dorofy."
