Drusila,f,,"Spanish (Latin American, Rare)|Portuguese (Brazilian, Rare)|Biblical Spanish|Biblical Portuguese",,,,,,,,Spanish and Portuguese form of Drusilla.
Drusille,f,,French (African),/dʁy.sil/(African French),,,,,,,French form of Drusilla.
Drustanus,m,,Old Celtic (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Drustan. It appears in a 6th-century tombstone inscription (“Drustanus lies here, the son of Cunomorus”) and many scholars have thought to identify Drustanus with the Tristan of Celtic legend. (On the other hand, other evidence suggests that Tristan is actually based on the 8th-century Drust, son of a Pictish king, and not this Drustanus.)"
Drusticc,f,,Pictish,,,,,,,,6th century Pictish princess. Feminine variant of the name Drust. Older form or variant of the name Trista
Drutalos,m,,Gaulish,,,,,,,,"Derived from Gaulish *deruos / derua ""oak tree"" and talu- ""forehead; front; surface""."
Druva,f,,Sanskrit,Droo-vuh,,,,,,,Not available.
Druvis,m,,Latvian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Latvian druva ""cornfield""."
