Druward,m,,Anglo-Norman,,,,,,,,"Possibly from Old French Droart, Drouart which is probably from the hypothetical Germanic name *Droghard, itself composed of the element drog of uncertain meaning (see Drogo) combined with hard ""hard, firm, brave, strong""."
