Du,,"杜, 都, 度, etc.(Chinese)",Vietnamese|Chinese,/zu˧˧/|/jʊw˧˧/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 攸 (du) meaning ""distant, far"", 遊 (du) meaning ""to roam, travel"", or 瑜 (du) meaning ""fine jade"". A famous bearer was the poet Nguyễn Du (阮攸) (1766-1820), who wrote the epic poem Truyện Kiều."
Dũ,m,,Vietnamese,/zu˦ˀ˥/|/jʊw˧˨/|/jʊw˨˩˦/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 愈 (dũ) meaning ""more; to surpass, exceed""."
Dụ,m,,Vietnamese,/zu˧˨ʔ/|/jʊw˨˩ʔ/|/jʊw˨˩˨/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 諭 (dụ) meaning ""instruct, tell, make known"" or 裕 (dụ) meaning ""abundant, rich, plentiful""."
Dư,,,Vietnamese,/zɨ˧˧/|/jɨ˧˧/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 餘 (dư) meaning ""surplus, excess, remainder"", 璵 (dư) meaning ""beautiful jade"", or 輿 (dư) meaning ""cart, earth, public""."
Dự,m,,Vietnamese,/zɨ˧˨ʔ/|/jɨ˨˩ʔ/|/jɨ˨˩˨/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 譽 (dự) meaning ""fame, reputation, to praise""."
