Duimelijntje,f,,Folklore,dui-mə-LAYN-tyə,,,,,,,"Dutch form of Thumbelina, which is derived from Dutch duim meaning ""thumb"" combined with the Dutch diminutive suffixes -lijn and -tje."
Duinn,m,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Duinn, or Donn is the mythological Lord of the Dead and an ancestor of the Gaels in Irish mythology. Known as ""the dark one,"" he was said to reside at Tech Duinn (the House of Donn), an island gateway off the southwestern coast of Ireland where souls gather.Donn was one of the legendary Milesian brothers who invaded Ireland. After mocking a local goddess, he drowned in a storm before fully reaching the land. His spirit was the first to inhabit the Otherworld, making him the supreme gatekeeper and guide for the departed.Over time, he became a fairy king and phantom horseman. His domain is typically identified as Bull Rock off the Beara Peninsula in County Cork, Ireland."
