Eadhild,f,,Anglo-Saxon|History,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old English ead ""wealth, fortune"" combined with Old English hild ""battle"". Cognate to Audhild.This name was borne by the second wife of the 10th-century Frankish duke Hugh the Great, who was a daughter of the Anglo-Saxon king Edward the Elder."
