Egron,m,,Swedish,,,,,,,,"Relatively modern name (first used in 1815) meaning ""own the calm"" or ""own the peace"". A notable bearer, and also the first bearer, was Swedish painter Egron Sellif Lundgren (1815-1875) whose father named him after the phrase äg ron (och ett) sällt liv meaning ""own the calm (and a) happy life"". Egron is also Norge ""Norway"" spelled backwards, though this is probably a coincidence."
