Eidothea,f,Εἰδοθέα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from either εἶδος (eidos) meaning ""appearance, shape, form"" or perhaps εἰδώς (eidos) meaning ""who knows, initiates, is knowledgeable"" (participle of οἶδα ""to know""), combined with θεά (thea) meaning ""goddess"". This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including an Oceanid, and a former name of the goddess Theonoe"
