Elacrab,m,,Astronomy,/ɛl.ˈæk.ræb/,,,,,,,"Elacrab is a name of a star in constellation Scorpius, also known as Beta Scorpii. Beta Scorpii bore the traditional names Acrab, Akrab or Elacrab, all deriving from the Arabic name (Arabic: العقرب‎) al-'Aqrab ""the Scorpion"""
El'ad,m,אֶלְעָד(Hebrew),Hebrew,/ʔel.ˈad/|/ʔel.ˈʔad/,,,,,,,"Means ""God is an eternity"" in Hebrew, from אֵל (ʾēl) ""God, the supreme deity, esp. the God of Israel"" and עַד (ʿaḏ) ""an eternity"".See also the Hebrew name Adel, which uses the same elements but in reverse order (cf. Nathanael and Elnathan for another Hebrew example of this phenomenon).In the Bible ʾElʿāḏ was a member of the Tribe of Ephraim who was murdered by the Gat people.Elad is also the name of a large settlement in central Israel."
