Elban,f,,Turkish (Archaic),el-BAHN,,,,,,,"Etymologically composed of the Turkic element il or el meaning ""state, realm, people"" and the archaic agent/protective suffix -ban (allied to -van or -man). Historically, it signified a land-owning citizen who was fiercely loyal, protected, and bound to the state's laws. In contemporary times, its meaning has shifted to mean ""loyal to the country, protector of the homeland""."
