Eldem,f,,Turkish,el-DEHM,,,,,,,"A Turkish name composed of the root el (meaning ""hand"" or ""people/community"") and the old nominalizing suffix -dem. It indicates someone who is ""gentle, amiable, familiar, well-mannered, and highly altruistic"". In philosophical terms, it functions as the native Turkic counterpart to the Ottoman/Persian concept of diğerkâm (selfless, empathetic), embodying the gentle symbol of ""quiet benevolence"" and ""communal devotion""."
