Eldlilja,f,,"Icelandic (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Means ""orange lily"" (species Lilium bulbiferum), literally ""fire lily"" in Icelandic, derived from the Old Norse elements eldr ""fire"" and lilja ""lily"". In Swedish, eldlilja instead refers to the species Lilium davidii."
