Elegast,m,,Carolingian Cycle|Literature|Dutch (Rare),/ˈe.lə.ɣɑst/(Dutch),,,,,,,"Means ""noble guest"", derived from the Middle Dutch adjective edel meaning ""noble"" combined with the Middle Dutch noun gast meaning ""guest"".In medieval Dutch literature, this is the name of the eponymous character of Karel ende Elegast (""Charles and Elegast""), a 13th-century epic poem about Charlemagne and his friend, the noble knight Elegast."
