Elfin,m,,Medieval English (?)|History (Ecclesiastical)|Medieval Welsh,,,,,,,,"This was the name of an obscure local saint venerated in medieval Warrington, a town in the Anglo-Saxon kingdom of Mercia. It is allegedly a British derivative of Latin Alpinus (see Alpin; also Elphin, Alvin)."
Elfine,f,,Literature|English (Rare),EL-feen|el-FEEN,,,,,,,"Perhaps an invented name based on similar-sounding names such as Elvina, Elfa and Elfreda, influenced by the word elfin. It was coined in the 19th century, when many Old English names were revived. Elfine Starkadder is a character in Stella Gibbons' comic novel 'Cold Comfort Farm' (1932)."
