Elgitha,f,,English|Medieval English|Literature,EL-gə-thə(English),,,,,,,"From a medieval form of any of the Old English names Ælfgyð, Æðelgyð or Ealdgyð. This was used by Sir Walter Scott for a character in his novel Ivanhoe (1819)."
