Eliasaf,m,אליאסף(Hebrew),Hebrew (Rare)|Biblical Spanish,EH-LEE-AH-SAHF,,,,,,,"Combination of Eli 2 and Asaf 1; means ""my God has collected"" or ""my God gathers"" in Hebrew.This name is not to be confused with אליסף (see Elyasaf), which is spelled differently in Hebrew, and comes from the biblical name Eliasaph."
Eliasaph,m,אֶלְיָסָף(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""God has added"" or ""God increases (the family)"" in Hebrew, derived from Hebrew אֵל (ʾel) ""God"" and יָסַף (yasaf) ""to add"". This was the name of two minor biblical characters; one was a son of Deuel, and the other was a son of Lael."
Eliaser,m,,Greenlandic,,,,,,,,Greenlandic form of Elieser.
Eliashib,m,אֶלְיָשִׁיב(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""El restores"" or ""El causes to return."" The name of multiple men in the Bible, including three men who were forced to divorce their foreign wives after the Ezrahite return to Jerusalem. It was also the name of a high priest around the same time."
Ê-li-a-síp,m,,Biblical Vietnamese,,,,,,,,Vietnamese form of Eliashib.
