Elwing,f,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Means ""foam of stars"" or ""star-spray"" from Sindarin êl ""star"" and gwing ""foam, spindrift, spume, (flying) spray blown off wave-tops"". In 'The Lord of the Rings' (1954) J. R. R. Tolkien, Elwing was a daughter of Dior, named for the waterfall of Lanthir Lamath in Ossiriand; she was also the mother of Elrond and grandmother of Arwen."
