Elysande,f,,Germanic,əl-ee-sahnd,,,,,,,"A medieval Germanic name, meaning ""temple path,"" that likely originates from Visigothic elements: alah, signifying temple or hall, and sind, denoting path, travel, journey, or way. It is among several variants of the name Alasind, with alternative spellings such as Elisende, Elisenda, Elysant, Elisent, and Helisent."
