Élysée,f,,French,EH-LEE-ZEH,,,,,,,"In this spelling, the name is probably intended as a French form of Elysia.However, it more likely arose as a modern feminine form of Élisée, the French form of Eliseus.The name is most famously known as that of the Avenue des Champs-Élysées and the Palais de l'Élysée, where the French president resides."
