Emathion,m,Ἠμαθίων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ἠμαθία (Emathia), the name of an ancient region of Macedonia possibly derived from the Homeric Greek word ἠμαθόεις (emathoeis) meaning ""sandy"", which is ultimately derived from ἄμαθος (amathos) meaning ""sand, dust, sandy soil"". Emathion was the name of several characters in Greek mythology, one of them being a Samothracian king and son of Zeus who in some accounts is the eponym of Emathia."
