Enceladus,m,Ἐγκέλαδος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""making noise, rushing"", derived from Ancient Greek ἐν (en) meaning ""in"" and κέλαδος (kelados) meaning ""loud noise, shout, clamour"". This was the name of one of the Giants or Gigantes in Greek mythology, traditionally an opponent of Athena. A moon of Saturn is named after him. Enceladus was also the name of a son of King Aegyptus, killed by his wife (named either Trite or Amymone) on their wedding night."
