Engelke,,,Dutch (Rare)|West Frisian (Rare)|North Frisian (Rare)|East Frisian (Rare)|Low German (Rare),"ENG-əl-kə(Dutch, West Frisian)",,,,,,,"In the case of male bearers, this name is a diminutive of Engel. In the case of female bearers, this name is a feminine form of Engel. Also compare Engeltje.In the Netherlands, the name is frequently associated with the Dutch word engelke, which is an older form of the word engeltje and means ""little angel""."
