Éovin,f,,Literature (?),,,,,,,,"Hungarian form of Éowyn, a character created by J. R. R. Tolkien for his 'Lord of the Rings' books, meaning ""horse lover""."
Eowa,m,,"Anglo-Saxon (Anglicized, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Eowa is a name found to have been in use during the time of the kingdom of Mercia.Sources state that Eowa was a king of the Mercians at the time of the Battle of Maserfield (or Cogwy), co-ruling between 634 - 642. He was of the Dynasty Iclingas."
Eowyn,f,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Éowyn.
