Epagathos,m,Ἐπάγαθος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""valliant, true"", derived from Greek ἐπί (epi) meaning ""on"" and ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good""."
Epagathus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Epagathos.
Epainetos,m,Ἐπαίνετος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Biblical Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἐπαινετός (epainetos) meaning ""praised, praiseworthy, laudable"", itself a derivative of ἔπαινος (epainos) meaning ""approval, praise, commendation"", ultimately composed of (epi) ""on, upon"" and αἶνος (ainos) ""praise; tale, story"". Also compare αἰνετός (ainetos) ""praiseworthy"".This was the name of an early Christian saint, mentioned in Paul's epistle to the Romans in the New Testament and considered one of the seventy disciples."
Epainista,f,Ἐπαινίστα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἔπαινος (epainos) meaning ""commendation, praise"" and the suffix ιστής (istes) meaning ""concerned with, one who is""."
Epalahame,m,,Tongan,,,,,,,,Tongan form of Abraham.
Epalame,m,,Tongan,,,,,,,,Contracted ford of Epalahame.
Epameinon,m,Ἐπαμείνων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἐπί (epi) meaning ""on, upon, towards"" and ἀμείνων (ameinon) meaning ""better""."
Epameinondas,m,Ἐπαμεινώνδας(Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek,,,,,,,,"Patronymic form of Epameinon using ίδας (idas), the West Greek form of ἴδης (ides). This was the name of a 4th-century BC Theban statesman and general."
Epaminonda,m,"Епаминонда(Macedonian, Serbian)",Croatian (Rare)|Italian (Rare)|Macedonian (Rare)|Romanian (Rare)|Serbian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Croatian, Italian, Macedonian, Romanian and Serbian form of Epameinondas via its latinized form Epaminondas."
Epaminondas,m,Ἐπαμεινώνδας(Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek|Portuguese (Brazilian),E-pah-mee-non-dahs(Greek),,,,,,,"Latinized form and modern Greek transcription of Epameinondas. This name was borne by a general and statesman of 4th-century BC Greece who transformed the ancient Greek city-state of Thebes, leading it out of Spartan subjugation into a preeminent position in Greek politics. The name is still used in modern-day Greece."
Epander,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History,,,,,,,,Latinized form of Epandros. This was the name of an Indo-Greek king from the 1st century BC.
Epandros,m,Ἔπανδρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""manly, befitting a man, virile"" in Ancient Greek, composed of ἐπί (epi) ""upon, on"" combined with ἀνδρός (andros) ""of a man""."
Epaphra,f,,Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Epaphrodita.
