Eparchis,f,Ἐπαρχίς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἐπάρχω (eparcho) meaning ""to govern, lead, rule over"" or ""to serve, offer, pour libations"", composed of ἐπί (epi) ""over, above"" and ἄρχω (archo) ""to lead, rule"" (see archos)."
Epari,m,,Manipuri,,,,,,,,"Means ""only son"" in Meitei."
