Equality,,,English (Rare),/ɪ.ˈkwɑ.lɪ.ti/(American English)|/ɪ.ˈkwɒl.ɪ.ti/(British English),,,,,,,"From the English word equality, borrowed from Middle French equalité 'equality'."
Equally,f,,Romani (Archaic),,,,,,,,Corruption of Aquilla.
Equanimeous,m,,African American (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Latin aequus “equal” and animus “mind”, meaning ""calm and composed, equanimous""."
Equaq,m,,Greenlandic,,,,,,,,Younger form of Eĸuaĸ.
Equila,,,Medieval Latin (?),,,,,,,,Not available.
