Equionte,m,,Portuguese (Rare),,,,,,,,Portuguese form of Echion.
Equitius,m,,Ancient Roman,/e.ˈkʷi.ti.us/(Latin)|/e.ˈkwi.t͡si.us/(Latin),,,,,,,"Meaning ""inhabitant of Aequi"", in modern-day Lazio. Famous bearers of this name include Flavius Equitius, a Roman consul, as well as two saints."
Equizio,m,,Italian,/e.ˈkwit.tsjo/,,,,,,,Italian form of Equitius.
