Ereleuva,f,,Gothic,,,,,,,,"Ereleuva was the mother of the Ostrogothic king Theoderic the Great. She is often referred to as the concubine of Theoderic's father, Theodemir, although that Gelasius refers to her as regina (""queen"") suggests that she had a prominent social position despite the informality of her union with Theodemir."
