Ereuthalion,m,Ἐρευθαλίων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἐρευθαλέος (ereuthaleos) meaning ""reddish, ruddy"", which is ultimately derived from ἔρευθος (ereuthos) meaning ""redness, flush"". Also compare ἐρεύθω (ereutho) ""to make red, to stain with red"" and ἐρυθρός (erythros) meaning ""red"". In Greek mythology, Ereuthalion was the name of several characters, one of them being the eponymous founder of the city Ereuthalia."
