Erginus,m,Ἐργῖνος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),/ˈɜːr.dʒɪ.nəs/(Greek Mythology)|/er.ɡîː.nos/(Attic Greek)|/er.ˈʝi.nos/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἔργον (ergon) meaning ""work, labour, deed"", or perhaps from ἔργω (ergo) meaning ""to enclose, shut in, bar one’s way"". This is the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including an Argonaut (sometimes called a son of Poseidon) and a Minyan king."
