Ergon,m,Ἔργον(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""work, labour, deed"" in Ancient Greek."
Ergophilos,m,Ἐργόφιλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἔργον (ergon) meaning ""work, task, deed"" combined with the Greek noun φίλος (philos) meaning ""friend, lover""."
Ergophilus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Ergophilos. This was the name of an Athenian strategos (military general) from the 4th century BC.
Ergoteles,m,Ἐργοτέλης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἔργον (ergon) meaning ""work, task, deed"" combined with the Greek noun τέλος (telos) meaning ""purpose, aim, goal"" as well as ""completion, accomplishment, fulfillment"" (see Aristotle).A known bearer of this name was the Olympic runner Ergoteles of Himera (5th century BC), who was originally from the island of Crete."
Ergotimos,m,Ἐργότιμος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἔργον (ergon) meaning ""work, task, deed"" combined with the Greek verb τιμάω (timao) meaning ""to honour, to esteem, to revere"".This was the name of an Athenian potter from the 6th century BC."
