Erianthe,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,"Popularly claimed to mean ""lover of flowers"" (apparently due to association with Greek eran ""to love, to be in love with""), it may actually mean ""woolly-haired flower"" from the botanical name eriantha, ultimately from Greek ἔριον (erion) ""wool"" and ανθος (anthos) ""flower""."
