Erina,f,Ерина(Macedonian),Italian (Swiss)|Italian|Macedonian|Irish (Rare)|English (Rare)|Dutch (Rare)|Afrikaans|Māori,eh-ree-na,,,,,,,"Originally a Swiss-Italian variant of Irene, its modern usage in Switzerland might be influenced by the name of the flower erinus alpinus, known in English as ""fairy foxglove"", ""starflower"" and ""alpine balsam"".In Italy, however, it is also occasionally considered a diminutive of Ero or Erio."
