Erkhembat,m,Эрхэмбат(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Mongolian эрхэм (erkhem) meaning ""important, supreme"" and бат (batu) meaning ""strong, firm""."
Erkhembayar,,Эрхэмбаяр(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Mongolian эрхэм (erkhem) meaning ""important, supreme"" and баяр (bayar) meaning ""celebration, joy""."
Erkhembuyan,,Эрхэмбуян(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Mongolian эрхэм (erkhem) meaning ""important, supreme"" and буян (buyan) meaning ""good deed, virtue, charity"" or ""fortune, blessing""."
Erkhemjamts,m,Эрхэмжамц(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Derives from Mongolian эрхэм (erkhem) meaning ""important, supreme"" and жамц (jamts) meaning ""rock"".A famous bearer is Erkhemjamts Luvsangiin (b. 1943), a former Mongolian cyclist. He competed in the individual road race and team time trial events at the 1964 Summer Olympics."
