Ertin,m,,Turkish,/er-tin/,,,,,,,"Ertin is a philosophical construction composed of Er (""early, valiant, man"") and Tin (""spirit, soul, essence""). It translates to ""the early awakened soul"" or ""the valiant essence."" Symbolically, it represents ""the convergence of raw physical strength and the internal, eternal breath of life."" It is a name for one who acts with ""the wisdom of the ancestors and the vitality of the morning."""
