Ešarra-ḫammat,f,,Ancient Assyrian,,,,,,,,"Translates to ""Ešarra is mistress"" but can be interpreted as ""Mullissu of Ešarra is mistress"", or possibly ""In Ešarra, Mullissu is mistress"". Ešarra was a temple and a cosmic realm in Mesopotamian cosmology. The only bearer of this name was Ešarra-ḫammat, a queen of the Neo-Assyrian empire as the wife of Esarhaddon."
