Esege,m,Эсеге(Mongolian Cyrillic)|Эсэгэ(Buryat Cyrillic),Mongolian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Esege Malan (Mongolian: Эсеге Малан, Buryat: Эсэгэ, Russian: Эсэгэ Малан), according to Mongol myth and the belief of the Buryats, is the great Creator of all living things. He is a Buryat sky-god who rules over the western horizon. His son is Solobung Yubin, a spiritual morning star which, if offered sacrifices, will reward the Mongol people with greater harvest yields and prosperity.As chief of the sky-spirits, Esege Malaan calls meetings of them ""in the Pleiades and on the moon"". Esege is a bald god."
