Euchenor,m,Εὐχήνωρ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,/eu̯.khɛ̌ː.nɔːr/(Attic Greek)|/eɸ.ˈçi.nor/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek εὐχή (euche) meaning ""prayer, wish, vow"" combined with ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man"". This is the name of several characters from Greek mythology, including one of the fifty sons of King Aegyptus, killed by his wife, Iphimedusa, on their wedding night."
