Eudamidas,m,Εὐδαμίδας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|History,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Eudamos"" in Greek, derived from the name Eudamos combined with ίδας (idas), which is the Aeolic and Doric Greek form of the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).This name was borne by three kings of Sparta, the earliest of which lived in the 4th century BC."
Eudamos,m,"Εὔδαμος, Εὐδάμος(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Doric Greek form of Eudemos, because it contains δᾶμος (damos), which is the Doric Greek form of δῆμος (demos) meaning ""people"" as well as ""country, land"".This name was borne by an Olympic victor from the Greek island of Kos (92 BC)."
Eudamus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Eudamos. A known bearer of this name was Eudamus of Cos, the Olympic winner of the Stadion race in 92 BC."
Euddogwy,m,,Medieval Welsh,,,,,,,,Euddogwy is the name of a 6th century male Welsh saint. His name is sometimes Latinized as Oudoceus.
