Eugnostos,m,Εὔγνωστος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek εὔγνωστος (eugnostos) meaning ""well-known, familiar"", composed of the elements εὖ (eu) ""good"" and γνωστός (gnostos) ""known, familiar"". Eugnostos the Blessed was the author of the Epistle of Eugnostos (ca. late 1st century), a Gnostic epistle found in Codices III and V of the Nag Hammadi library."
