Eugraphius,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Eugraphios. This name was borne by a Latin grammarian and author who probably lived in the 6th century AD.
Eugraphos,m,,Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Basically means ""well-drawn"" or ""well-written"", derived from Greek ευ (eu) meaning ""good, well"" combined with the Greek noun γράφος (graphos) meaning ""that which is drawn or written"" (i.e. writing, drawing). The latter element is ultimately derived from the Greek verb γράφειν (graphein) meaning ""to write, to draw""."
Eugraphus,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Eugraphos. A known bearer of this name was Eugraphus of Alexandria, a Christian martyr from the 4th century AD."
