Eusorus,m,"Εύσωρος, Εὔσωρος(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""having good corn"", derived from Ancient Greek εὖ (eu) meaning ""good, well"" and σωρός (soros)# meaning ""heap, pile (especially of corn); quantity"". Eusorus is mentioned several times in Greek mythology as the father of various characters."
