Eustochia,f,,Polish (Archaic)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"From a Greek word meaning ""well-aimed"", derived from εὖ (eu) ""good"" and στόχος (stochos) ""an aim, shot"". This was borne by Saint Eustochia Calafato, a 15th-century nun from Sicily."
Eustochio,m,,Italian,ew-STOH-kyoh,,,,,,,Masculine form of Eustochios.
Eustochium,f,,Late Roman,,,,,,,,4th century Christian ascetic and Desert Mother
Eustolia,f,Εὐστολία(Ancient Greek),Late Greek|Spanish (Mexican)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,Feminine form of Eustolios. This name was borne by a saint from the 7th century AD.
Eustolie,f,,"French (Archaic)|French (Quebec, Archaic)|History (Ecclesiastical)",,,,,,,,French form of Eustolia.
