Eustolos,m,Εὔστολος(Ancient Greek),Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective εὔστολος (eustolos), which is equivalent to the Greek adjective εὐσταλής (eustales) meaning ""well-equipped"". Also compare the Greek nouns στολή (stole) and στόλος (stolos), which both mean ""equipment"".A notable bearer of this name was Eustolos of Side (also Sidon), an Olympic victor from 113 AD. His name has also been recorded as Εὔσταλος (Eustalos)."
Eustolus,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Eustolos.
