Evanassa,f,Εὐάνασσα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"From Greek Εὐάνασσα (Euanassa), composed of the elements εὖ (eu) meaning ""good"" and ἄνασσα (anassa) meaning ""queen, lady"" (the feminine form of ἄναξ (anax) ""master, lord""). This was an epithet of the goddess Demeter."
