Evangelio,m,,"Italian (Archaic)|Spanish (Latin American, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Italian and Spanish form of Evangelius. It should be noted that in Spanish-speaking countries, the name can also be derived from the Spanish noun evangelio meaning ""(the) Gospel"", which is etymologically related to the aforementioned name."
Évangélique,f,,"French (Rare)|French (African, Rare)|French (Quebec, Rare)|French (Belgian, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Derived from the French adjective évangélique meaning ""evangelical"". In other words, this name is the French feminine form of Evangelicus.Also compare similar religious names, such as Évangéliste and Évangèle."
