Evangelus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Εὐάγγελος (Euangelos), which is the ancient Greek form of Evangelos.This name was borne by an ancient Greek comic poet from around the 3rd century BC: his original name was Euangelos, but he is more often referred to by the latinized forms of his name, namely this one and Euangelus. In later times, the name Evangelus is also regularly used to refer to the martyr and saint Evangelicus of Tomis, who lived in the 3rd century AD."
