Evoleht,f,,"English (Modern, Rare)",/ˈɛv.ə.lɛt/,,,,,,,"Variant of Evolet, altered to be the phrase the love spelled backwards. Since 2010 this name has been given to 171 girls born in the United States. Additionally, there was one girl named Evoleht in the national records of Scotland 2018."
Evolet,f,,Popular Culture|English (Modern),/ˈɛv.ə.lɛt/,,,,,,,"Created for the 2008 movie 10,000 B.C., which was directed, produced and co-written by Roland Emmerich. In the movie Evolet is a prehistoric woman whose name means ""the promise of life"" in the fictitious language spoken by her adopted tribe, the Yaghal.It has been suggested that the name was created from an elaboration of love as a palindrome, or from the phrase t(h)e love spelled backwards with the H omitted for the sake of aesthetics (also see Evoleht), or from the word evolve as an incomplete anagram. It could also be viewed as a combination of the names Evelyn and Violet."
