Fantasy,f,,American (Rare),/ˈfæn.tə.si/,,,,,,,"Directly taken from the Engish word fantasy, which was ultimately derived from Old French fantasie (“fantasy”), from Latin phantasia (“imagination”), from Ancient Greek φαντασία (phantasía, “apparition”). This word is basically a doublet of Fancy (see also Fantasia)."
