Faramarz,m,فرامرز(Persian),Persian Mythology|Persian,/fæ.ɾɒː.ˈmæɾz/(Persian),,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly derived from Persian آمرزیدن (āmorzidan) meaning ""to forgive"". This is the name of a hero (a son of Rostam) in the 10th-century epic the Shahnameh."
Faramir,m,,Literature,FAH-rah-meer,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. Probably ""sufficient jewel"" from the Sindarin far meaning ""sufficient, adequate"" and mir meaning ""jewel, precious thing."" In J.R.R. Tolkien's 'The Lord of the Rings', Faramir was the son of Denethor, brother of Boromir, and eventual husband of Eowyn."
