Favorinus,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Roman cognomen from Latin favor ""goodwill, inclination, partiality"", derived from faveo ""to favor"", with an adjective-forming suffix. Favorinus (80–160) was a Roman sophist and skeptic philosopher who flourished during the reign of Hadrian and the Second Sophistic."
