Finis,m,,American (South),FIE-nis,,,,,,,"Means ""end"" in Latin. This was the middle name of Jefferson Davis (1808-1889), leader of the Confederacy during the American Civil War, who was the last of his parents' ten children. It was first used as a given name in his honour, in the American South."
Finita,f,,Spanish|Spanish,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Josefa.
