Finnja,f,,German (Modern),FIN-ya,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown, possibly a form of Finya.It is unclear whether this name was actually inspired by the same-sounding Russian nickname Finya or whether it was invented independently in Germany, by combining the popular masculine name Finn 1 or Finn 2 with the popular suffix ja.The name does not have a Scandinavian etymology and is not popular in any Scandinavian country."
