Floria,f,,Late Roman|Dutch (Rare)|German (Rare)|Italian|Spanish|English (Rare)|Medieval English|Theatre|Judeo-Anglo-Norman|Judeo-French|Albanian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Florius.Known bearers of this name include the Italian-born Canadian filmmaker Floria Sigismondi (b. 1965), the Venezuelan singer and actress Floria Márquez (b. 1950) and the Argentine actress Floria Bloise (1929-2012).Floria Tosca is also the name of the main character in Puccini's opera 'Tosca' (1900)."
Florià,m,,Catalan,,,,,,,,Catalan form of Florianus.
Floriaan,m,,Dutch (Rare),FLO-ree-a:n,,,,,,,Dutch form of Florianus (see Florian).
Florian,m,,Albanian,,,,,,,,Variant of Flori.
