Floscellus,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin floscellus, a diminutive of flosculus (which itself is a diminutive of flos ""flower, blossom""), meaning ""small flower"". Saint Floscellus was a young man who was martyred in the persecutions of Marcus Aurelius. He was tortured and thrown to wild animals in 2nd century at Autun, France."
