Forbflaith,f,,Medieval Irish|Medieval Scottish,,,,,,,,"Gaelic name which meant ""overlordship"" and ""overlord, ruler, sovereign"", derived from Old Irish fír ""true"" and flaith ""ruler; sovereignty"" (compare Gormlaith, Órfhlaith, Talulla). This was borne by one of the two heiresses of an early 13th-century earl of Atholl in Scotland."
