Fundana,f,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Feminine form of the cognomen Fundanus. It was borne by Galeria, a wife of Vitellius."
Fundanus,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Roman cognomen meaning ""of Fundi."" This name was borne by the suffect consul Gaius Minicius Fundanus in AD 107."
Fundin,m,,Old Swedish,,,,,,,,"Variant of Fundinn meaning ""foundling"" in Old Norse."
